#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Hub start, takeover and handoff, one command each.

  hub start    --stage retro-fixes --goal "<what the stage delivers>" --session <session id> [--name "Hub retro-fixes #1"]
               [--take-main-merge]
               [--skip-lock RESOURCE ...] [--dry-run] [--repo PATH | --no-project]
  hub takeover --stage stage-a --session <session id> [--n 17] [--handoff PATH] [--dry-run]
               [--name "Hub stage-a #17"] [--goal "…"] [--skip-lock RESOURCE ...] [--take-main-merge]
               [--main-merge-until +30d] [--repo PATH | --no-project]
  hub handoff  --stage stage-a [--n 16] [--out PATH] [--session ID] [--allow-live-subagents] [--owner-asked]
  hub handoff  --stage stage-a --finish [--handoff PATH] [--allow-todo]
  hub succeed  --stage stage-a --handoff PATH [--allow-todo] [--model M] [--effort E] [--permission-mode MODE] [--cwd DIR] [--headless] [--dry-run] [--owner-asked]
  hub succeed  --stage stage-a --fallback [--why TEXT]
  hub succeed  --stage stage-a --replace [--force] [--handoff PATH] [--dry-run]
  hub grilling start|end|status [--stage stage-a] [--session ID] [--topic TEXT] [--why TEXT]
  hub rename   --stage OLD --to NEW [--dry-run]
  hub close    --stage stage-a [--why TEXT] [--force] [--dry-run]
  hub effort   [--session ID] [--json]
  hub reviewer [--for CLASS] [--author ROLE|ENGINE[/MODEL]] [--stage stage-a] [--json] [--all]
  hub grill    [open] --stage stage-a [--questions ID,…] [--also-stage S] [--topic T] [--owner-words T]
               [--host auto|desktop|codex-app|bg|manual] [--model M] [--effort E] [--again] [--dry-run]
  hub grill    bind --stage stage-a --launch ID --session FULL_ID
  hub grill    join --stage stage-a --launch ID --session self  |  hub grill done --stage stage-a --summary "…" [--why …]
  hub home     [--cwd DIR] [--json]
  hub home migrate [--from DIR] [--to DIR] [--apply]
Every subcommand takes --stage (default $HUB_STAGE); start, takeover, handoff, succeed, rename, close and grill need a stage, `reviewer`
puts it into the `agent spawn` line it prints, `home` and `effort` ignore it, `grilling` finds it from the session.

start registers the first hub of a new stage: it creates <hub home>/<stage>/ and then runs the takeover steps
below with no predecessor (hub #1, tag hub-1). It refuses a stage that already has a hub or a handoff — that is a
takeover. It refuses (exit 2) a stage name that carries no word about the work — only generic words (hub, stage, wave,
wp, task, work, test, tmp, new, default, stream, sprint; $AGENT_HUB_GENERIC_STAGE_WORDS replaces the list), numbers and
single letters, like `hub-09`, `stage-2`, `wave-a` — and a start without --goal "<one line: what the stage delivers>".
The goal is kept in <stage dir>/stage.json; the hub's registered title becomes "Hub <stage> #N — <goal>" (trimmed), and
takeover, succeed, the handoff draft, the digest and agent-top carry it. A stage without a goal keeps "Hub <stage> #N";
takeover never refuses on the name, and takeover --goal sets or replaces the goal. AGENT_HUB_NO_NAMING=1 in the
environment (scripted environments, the test suite) skips both start checks. It warns (ATTENTION lines, once) when the
hub home is the legacy ~/.claude/agent-hub (`hub home`), when the
Claude Code CLI is older than 2.1.287 (the minimum supported; its model aliases resolve to older models) and when a command of the same name as one of the plugin's tools (any executable of its
bin/: hub, jlog, jwait, agent, ask, roles, lock, …) comes first on PATH, GitHub CLI `hub` from Homebrew being the
usual one.

rename moves a stage to a new name when none of its agents is alive (otherwise it exits 2 and lists the live ones): the
directory, the names and paths in the stage's json files (roles.json, agents/*/meta.json, stage.json), the question
register's heading and the board's lock notes that name the stage. The new name is checked like start's. --dry-run lists
what would change. Logs, journals and briefs keep their text; run it between shifts, a session still running under
HUB_STAGE=OLD keeps the old name.

close ends a stage whose hub is no longer needed (the work is delivered or dropped). It refuses (exit 2, the lines
listed) while an agent of the stage runs (`agent stop --stage S <role>`) or an owner question still waits (`ask close` /
`ask withdraw`); --force stops those agents through `agent stop` and leaves the questions in the register. Then: the
hub's session as in takeover step 4 (an idle background session is stopped, history kept; a busy, Desktop or terminal
one is named in an ATTENTION line with how to end it, also in the first line of the output — a Desktop hub is archived in
Desktop); every lock held by a session of the stage's roles (and of the agents it stopped) is released. A session that
still plays a live role in another open stage — or may: a registry of another stage could not be read — keeps its
locks and is not stopped. Then, under the stage's roles lock: every role is retired ("stage closed: <why>"; `roles list
--all` keeps them), a journal line "[<tag>] close: …" and, last, <stage dir>/stage.json gets "closed": {at, why, by,
hub}; a takeover that registered a new hub while the close ran wins (nothing retired, exit 1). `agent spawn` refuses a
closed stage. A closed stage is left out of agent-top (`--all` shows it),
the watchdog, the night queue and the owner-question summaries (`ask list --stage S` still reads it); its files stay.
`hub takeover` (or `hub start`) on a closed stage reopens it and says so in its start line. A re-run after a failed step
finishes the close; on a closed stage it prints when and why and exits 0. --dry-run lists the steps and writes nothing.

The shift number is derived: takeover = the registered hub's number (roles `hub`, tag hub-N) + 1, or the
successor named in the latest handoff ("… → \"Hub <stage> #N\""); handoff = the registered hub's number.
--n overrides both (a re-run of a takeover finds itself registered and keeps its number).

--session is the new hub's own session: a Claude Desktop id (local_…, looked up in the Desktop session
metadata for its CLI id and title) or a Claude Code CLI session uuid ($CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID); `self` = the session
running the command ($CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID read by the tool, so the command line holds no shell expansion and an
allow rule `Bash(hub takeover:*)` matches it).

Where a hub runs (start and takeover; checked first, before anything is registered, journaled or locked): in a linked
worktree of its project that has the project's .agent-hub/ — not in the project's main clone, which has whatever branch
somebody checked out there, and not outside git (a Claude Desktop session started under "No folder" runs in ~ or a temp
dir). The project is the repository of --repo PATH (any path inside it), else of the working directory, else the stage's
recorded one (<hub home>/<stage>/stage.json, written by every successful start and takeover in a repository);
--no-project, for a stage that has no repository, starts in place (the start line says so; recorded for the stage's
later hubs, replacing a recorded repo: the latest choice wins); AGENT_HUB_NO_PROJECT=1 in the environment, for scripted environments and the test suite, does the same
silently. A good place is refreshed — a clean worktree with no commits of its own is fast-forwarded to origin's
default branch (origin/HEAD, else origin/main, else origin/master) after a bounded `git fetch` — and the command goes
on. Any other place gets a fresh worktree <repo>/.claude/worktrees/<stage>-hub-<n> on a new branch from that branch (a
clean one already there at that commit is reused, else the name gets -2, -3…; a failing fetch falls back to the local
ref with a note; without an origin: the local main/master), and the command prints `MOVE <path>`, how to move there
(Claude Code: EnterWorktree with path=<path>, else mcp__ccd_directory__change_directory with it; Codex: that workdir)
and the command line to re-run, and exits 4. With nothing that names a project it prints `NO PROJECT: …`, exit 4:
re-run with --repo <the project's main clone> or --no-project.

takeover, in order, each step verified, the first failed step stops with a message; a step whose
target state is already there is skipped as "already done", so a re-run finishes a broken takeover:
  1. locks: every active lock of the previous hub is taken over with `lock take --force`, keeping
     kind, repo, until and value. The previous hub is every session named by the roles entry `hub`
     or the `coordinator:` line of night-queue.md (other than the new one); when they disagree it
     says so and takes the locks of all of them. --take-main-merge also takes main-merge of the hub's
     repo (AGENT_HUB_DEFAULT_REPO, else the git repository you run in, else "*") when nobody holds it (until --main-merge-until) or when a third
     party (e.g. a merge steward, a hub of another stage) holds it, and prints an ATTENTION line naming the holder's stage and
     the age of its latest journal line; without the flag, and for other repos, a third-party holder is reported and left alone.
     AGENT_HUB_TAKE_MAIN_MERGE=true (repository config) makes the flag the default for a free lock and for a lock held by an
     earlier hub of this stage (a takeover); a lock held by anyone else, and any held lock on `start`, is left alone
     whatever the config says. The free lock is never added when a main-merge is already taken over or held (no second, wildcard
     record); without the flag a free main-merge of the configured hub repo is reported in the digest. --skip-lock RESOURCE
     (also on `start`) leaves that lock where it
     is (a sub-agent of the old hub still works under it).
  2. night-queue.md: `coordinator: <new session id>` (the night nudge addresses it) and `updated:`
     (single-line edits, atomic write). Skipped when the stage has no night queue.
  3. the project step: an executable takeover.sh from the config layers (<hub home>/<stage>/, the current
     repository's .agent-hub/, the hub home), run as `takeover.sh check` / `takeover.sh apply` with HUB_STAGE,
     HUB_N, HUB_TAG, HUB_NAME, HUB_SESSION, HUB_CLI_SESSION, HUB_PREVIOUS, HUB_TAKEOVER_AT, HUB_HANDOFF set.
  4. roles set hub <session> --tag hub-<n>. When the hub registered before is still running (`claude agents --json`;
     a `done` background session that keeps its pid counts), other hubs could still message it by name: a background
     session that is not busy is stopped (`claude stop <id>`, bounded; its history stays, `claude rm` is never run) and
     the output, the digest and the journal start line say so. A busy one, a Desktop session (archive it in Desktop; a
     Desktop hub does it with mcp__ccd_session_mgmt__archive_session), a terminal session, the session that runs the
     takeover and a stop that failed keep running: one ATTENTION line, also in the digest, names it and how to stop it.
     A CLI that does not answer is silent. A takeover by the registered hub's own number — the same shift taken again —
     writes "re-took shift #N (replaces <id8>), handoff by #M" and keeps one link in a lock's reason, not the nest of
     the earlier takeovers.
  5. jlog "[hub-<n>] start: …".
  Then prints a digest ≤ 3 KB: handoff § 0, the standing permissions in force for the stage and its repository,
  recorded in any stage's register (the first few, then "K more"; one line when there are none), the ask register (first line "awaiting execution: N (ids)" —
  owner answers without `ask done`; then open questions, recent owner answers and agent decisions — check
  every "owner said" of the handoff against it), locks, live roles with the age of their last journal
  line, and the command for the first `jwait` with --since = the handoff's mtime, so lines written
  during the handover are delivered.
  --dry-run prints the plan and the digest and writes nothing.
handoff writes a pre-filled HANDOFF-hub-<stage>-YYYY-MM-DD-HHMM.md with the facts filled in and TODO where the
hub must write; it releases nothing. Environment facts (versions, deploys, open PRs) come from an optional
executable handoff-facts.sh (config layers as above) that prints Markdown table rows "| What | State | Where it shows |".
Before writing the draft, handoff looks for sub-agents (the Agent tool) that are still running: those of the hub's
own session — --session, else the registered hub's, and the session running the command if that is another one. A
sub-agent dies with its parent session and the successor cannot message it. If any is live it lists them (id,
description, age) and the three ways out, and exits 2; with --allow-live-subagents it writes the draft with the list in
its TODO section.
handoff --finish is the last step of writing one: it checks the draft (--handoff, else the stage's latest) and refuses
(exit 2, the lines listed) while § 0–2 — the successor's first steps, the state, the queue — still hold TODO;
--allow-todo lets it through and says what stays open. `hub succeed --handoff` makes the same check before it starts
a successor, and `hub takeover` warns (ATTENTION) when the handoff it reads still has TODO in § 0–2.
succeed starts the successor of an automatic handoff (autopilot, AGENT_HUB_AUTO_HANDOFF; bin/autopilot.py): it checks the
chain (AGENT_HUB_AUTO_HANDOFF_CHAIN automatic handoffs in a row without the owner; at the limit it journals that and
exits 3), then starts `claude --bg --remote-control <stage>-hub-<n+1>` from the main checkout of --cwd (default: the
worktree the registered hub recorded at takeover, else here; outside git or in another project: refused, exit 2) in a new worktree
(`--worktree <stage>-hub-<n+1>`, a free name) with the hub's model and permission mode, an explicit
effort (--effort, AGENT_HUB_SUCCESSOR_EFFORT, else the effort this hub runs at now — `hub effort`; when that cannot be read,
succeed exits 1 and starts nothing) and the prompt "/delamain:hub take over stage … [agent-hub auto-handoff k/N]" (the marker keeps the name used before the rename for
one release), reads its id and Remote Control link,
journals both and prints the `jwait` command that waits for the successor's start line (AGENT_HUB_SUCCESSOR_TIMEOUT).
When the background session cannot start (CLI not logged in, the main checkout untrusted) it says so loudly (WARNING, in
the output and the journal: the successor is not listed in Claude Desktop) and starts a headless hub
with `agent spawn --cwd <main checkout> --worktree <stage>-hub-<n+1>` instead; bypassPermissions without its accepted disclaimer
becomes auto (acceptEdits for Haiku). --fallback, after the jwait's ALARM: journals the background session's log
tail, stops it and starts the headless hub from the same handoff. Only the registered hub may run it
($CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID, else $HUB_TAG; exit 2 otherwise; a sub-agent of the hub shares its session id and passes —
the hub never delegates it), only with AGENT_HUB_AUTO_HANDOFF on (exit 2; --force for the owner by hand), one
successor per shift: a second call while one is
being started or has not taken over is refused with the time to retry and a ready jwait; --again drops the record
of a successor that did not take over and is not running. --replace replaces the successor that already took over (or
runs): it stops it (`claude stop`, history kept; a busy one only with --force; a headless one with --force) and starts a
new one from the same handoff through the same code — the same number, model, mode and chain position, the same
--auto-handoff takeover command. Only the hub that handed over (the session recorded with the successor) or the owner at a
terminal may; nothing is stopped when the sessions cannot be listed. The successor's takeover carries --auto-handoff,
which keeps the chain; so does a takeover of the shift the pending successor already took over (its replacement, by hand
or by --replace); a hand-started session is recorded as kind `manual`, which `--replace` refuses to act on; any other
takeover resets it.
With --engine codex, --surface auto prepares a native desktop request in an actual app hub; the current app agent
executes native list_projects/create_thread and desktop-request/bind/fail/status only with an explicit human
creation request. Unavailable/unauthorized native creation retains the request and active predecessor until verified.
Actual takeover verifies its own identity/cwd and observed policy; APIs cannot set Full Access.
In an app hub, --surface cli or --headless requires the owner's AGENT_HUB_DESKTOP_CLI_HANDOFF opt-in in
the hub home's config.json (off by default); agent flags, environment and repository settings cannot grant it.
Terminal/detached CLI selection starts a detached Codex hub in its own worktree from the main checkout, preserving
model, effort and supported sandbox restrictions. It uses agent send and the captured result instead of Remote
Control. Full access maps to bypassing approvals and sandbox; native guards remain enabled (docs/codex.md).
grill launches a separate interactive session that grills the owner over the stage's open questions, records the answers
in the `ask` register and reports to the hub with one line "@hub GRILLED …" (bin/grill_session.py has the details):
open (default) writes the brief and launches by host — Claude Desktop: start_session arguments with initiation user_asked
for the hub to call; Codex app: create_thread arguments; another Claude host: `claude --bg --remote-control` and its link;
another Codex host: the command for the owner. bind records the full native launch result; join registers the new session as role `grill`; done reports and retires it.
grilling marks that the stage's hub is grilling the owner (bin/grilling.py): start, run by the hub before the first round
(in Claude Code the budget hook also marks it when the grilling skill loads), end once the topic's frontier is empty or
the owner stops it, status to show it. --session: the hub's session (default this one; the owner at a terminal: the
registered hub's); --stage, else the stage whose hub that session is. Only a registered hub's session is marked. While
the mark holds (until end, a takeover, or AGENT_HUB_GRILLING_STALE_MIN without an owner prompt), with the autopilot on,
succeed (a new successor, --again, --fallback) refuses, exit 2, unless --owner-asked — the owner asked for this handoff;
handoff (a draft) refuses the same way unless --owner-asked or the budget hook recorded the context ceiling, and a draft
written then gets a § 0 item to carry the grilling (topic, questions and answers with their `ask` ids, open frontier,
next round) for the successor to resume; a successor's `takeover --auto-handoff` waits too unless succeed ran with
--owner-asked.
effort prints the effort a Claude Code session runs at now and where it was read (bin/session_effort.py): the hook input,
$CLAUDE_EFFORT of the Bash tool, the last assistant record of the transcript, the `--effort` of a `claude --bg` session's
state.json, the Desktop session record, the CLI process argv — most current first; the first that answers wins and the
others that disagree are listed (the argv is fixed at launch, so it lags an in-session /effort). --session: a CLI session
uuid, a Desktop local_… id or `self` (default). --json prints every source's reading. Exit 0 with an answer, 1 when no
source answers (every source tried is named).
reviewer chooses the reviewer for a change: it walks the list AGENT_HUB_REVIEWERS (environment, a repository's
.agent-hub/config.json, the hub home's config.json; default one `agent` entry) and prints the first reviewer that is
available now — for the change class --for, if given — and exactly how to start it (bin/reviewers.py, docs/reviewers.md).
--all judges and lists every entry, with why not for the ones passed over; --json prints the same as JSON.
--author ROLE|ENGINE[/MODEL] names who wrote the change (a role of the stage — read from the agent's meta.json — or
claude|codex[/model]); the reviewer is chosen by it, not by the host's engine, and every `check` gets it as
AGENT_HUB_REVIEW_AUTHOR_ENGINE / AGENT_HUB_REVIEW_AUTHOR_MODEL. Without it the host's engine is assumed, and a line says so.
Exit 0 with a reviewer, 1 when none is available, 2 usage.
home prints where the hub keeps its files and why there: $AGENT_HUB_HOME, else a repository's .agent-hub/config.json
AGENT_HUB_HOME "project" (<main checkout>/.agent-hub/local/) or "user", else ~/agent-hub — the legacy ~/.claude/agent-hub
while ~/agent-hub does not exist; whether it is under a .claude directory (protected by Claude Code), and how to grant a
session access to it. home migrate moves the legacy home (--from) to the resolved one (--to): a dry run unless --apply,
which refuses while an agent or a background hub of the source runs, copies, verifies, rewrites the old path in the JSON files and renames the
source to <source>.migrated-YYYYMMDD (bin/hubhome.py). Exit 0 ok; a dry run exits 1 when --apply would refuse.
Exit: 0 ok, 1 step failed (reviewer: no reviewer available), 2 usage — or, for handoff, sub-agents of the hub's session
still running; succeed: 3 chain limit reached; start, takeover: 4 the session must move first (MOVE / NO PROJECT).
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import contextlib
import datetime as dt
import importlib.machinery
import importlib.util
import json
import os
import re
import shlex
import subprocess
import sys
import time
from pathlib import Path

sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)))
import autopilot  # noqa: E402
import grilling  # noqa: E402
import engines
import hubcore as hc  # noqa: E402
import grill_session  # noqa: E402
import hubhome  # noqa: E402
import reviewers  # noqa: E402
import session_effort  # noqa: E402
import subagents  # noqa: E402

DIGEST_BYTES = 3072
JWAIT_MATCH = hc.STATUS_WORDS  # the built-in wake words; digest --hub-events resolves hc.status_pattern() inside jwait
UUID_RE = re.compile(r"[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}")


def load_script(name: str):
    path = str(hc.BIN / name)
    loader = importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader(f"{name}_cli", path)
    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_loader(f"{name}_cli", loader)
    mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
    sys.modules[f"{name}_cli"] = mod  # dataclasses in `ask` look their module up here
    loader.exec_module(mod)
    return mod


def board_module():
    import board  # noqa: E402  (reads $AGENT_BOARD_FILE / $AGENT_HUB_HOME at import)
    return board


def ask_module():
    return load_script("ask")


def cut(text: str, limit: int, where: str = "") -> str:
    """Trim to `limit` UTF-8 bytes on a line boundary."""
    data = text.encode("utf-8")
    if len(data) <= limit:
        return text
    tail = f"\n…cut{', full text: ' + where if where else ''}"
    keep = data[: max(0, limit - len(tail.encode("utf-8")))].decode("utf-8", errors="ignore")
    if "\n" in keep:
        keep = keep[: keep.rfind("\n")]
    return keep + tail


def hub_name(stage: str, n: int) -> str:
    return f"Hub {stage} #{n}"


# a takeover's lock reason: "<name> <session>, took over from <who>: <reason>" — peeled back to <reason>
WHY_LINK_RE = re.compile(r"^.*?, (?:took over from|re-took shift)[^:]*: ")


def peel_why(why: str) -> str:
    while (m := WHY_LINK_RE.match(why)) is not None:
        why = why[m.end():]
    return why


HANDOFF_TITLE_RE = re.compile(r'^# Handoff "[^"\n]*#(\d+)" → "[^"\n]*#(\d+)"', re.MULTILINE)


def registered_hub(stage: str):
    """(number, record) of the hub in roles.json, or (None, record-or-None). The number is read from the tag:
    `hub-N`, a legacy `хаб-N`, any tag ending in `-N` (hc.hub_number)."""
    rec = hc.roles_load(stage)["roles"].get("hub")
    return hc.hub_number((rec or {}).get("tag")), rec


def handoff_numbers(path):
    """(outgoing, successor) from a handoff's title line, or (None, None)."""
    try:
        head = Path(path).read_text(encoding="utf-8")[:600]
    except (OSError, TypeError):
        return None, None
    m = HANDOFF_TITLE_RE.search(head)
    return (int(m.group(1)), int(m.group(2))) if m else (None, None)


def takeover_number(stage: str, session: str, cli: str, handoff, notes: list) -> int:
    """The new hub's number: kept on a re-run, else next_number()."""
    n, rec = registered_hub(stage)
    if n and (rec.get("session") in (session, cli) or rec.get("cli_session_id") == cli):
        return n
    return next_number(stage, handoff, notes)


def closed_next(stage: str):
    """The number after the hub of a closed stage (`hub close` retired it, stage.json keeps its tag), else None: the hub
    that reopens the stage does not reuse an old tag."""
    k = hc.hub_number((hc.stage_closed(stage) or {}).get("hub"))
    return k + 1 if k else None


def next_number(stage: str, handoff, notes: list, choose: str = "pass --n to choose") -> int:
    """The next hub's number: registered + 1, else the handoff's successor, else the closed hub's + 1, else 1 (the
    largest of them). `hub
    takeover` registers by it and `hub succeed` names its successor by it, so the name and the takeover agree."""
    n, _ = registered_hub(stage)
    from_roles = n + 1 if n else None
    _, from_handoff = handoff_numbers(handoff) if handoff else (None, None)
    if from_roles and from_handoff and from_roles != from_handoff:
        notes.append(f"roles say hub-{n} (next #{from_roles}), the handoff names #{from_handoff} — taking "
                     f"#{max(from_roles, from_handoff)}; {choose}")
    return max(x for x in (from_roles, from_handoff, closed_next(stage), 1) if x)


def handoff_number(stage: str, handoff=None, choose: str = "pass --n") -> int:
    """The current hub's number: registered, else the outgoing number of `handoff` (the one it wrote), else a guess —
    the successor named by the stage's latest handoff (the one this hub took over by)."""
    n, _ = registered_hub(stage)
    if n:
        return n
    out, _ = handoff_numbers(handoff) if handoff else (None, None)
    if out:
        return out
    _, succ = handoff_numbers(latest("HANDOFF-hub-*.md", stage))
    if succ:
        return succ
    raise hc.UsageError(f"no hub registered in stage {stage} (roles `hub`) and no handoff to count from — {choose}")


def coordinator_dir(stage: str) -> Path:
    return hc.root() / stage / "coordinator"


def latest(pattern: str, stage: str):
    files = sorted(coordinator_dir(stage).glob(pattern), key=lambda p: p.stat().st_mtime)
    return files[-1] if files else None


def section(text: str, number: int) -> str:
    m = re.search(rf"^## {number}\..*?(?=^## |\Z)", text, re.MULTILINE | re.DOTALL)
    return m.group(0).strip() if m else ""


def open_todos(text: str) -> list:
    """[(line number, line)] of the lines in § 0–2 of a handoff that still say TODO (what `hub handoff` writes where the
    hub must). The successor reads those sections first; § 3–6 are optional modules and loose ends. A TODO inside an
    HTML comment (the template's hints) is not one."""
    text = re.sub(r"<!--.*?-->", lambda m: "\n" * m.group(0).count("\n"), text, flags=re.DOTALL)  # keeps the line numbers
    found, current = [], None
    for lineno, line in enumerate(text.splitlines(), 1):
        m = re.match(r"## (\d+)\.", line)
        if m:
            current = int(m.group(1))
        if current is not None and current <= 2 and re.search(r"\bTODO\b", line):
            found.append((lineno, line.strip()))
    return found


def todo_report(todos: list, width: int = 110) -> str:
    return "\n".join(f"  line {n}: {ln[:width]}{'…' if len(ln) > width else ''}" for n, ln in todos[:12]) + (
        f"\n  … and {len(todos) - 12} more" if len(todos) > 12 else "")


def check_handoff_todos(handoff, allow: bool) -> None:
    """Refuse (a usage error, exit 2) a handoff whose § 0–2 still hold TODO, unless `allow`, which says what stays open."""
    try:
        todos = open_todos(Path(handoff).read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
    except OSError as e:
        raise hc.Failure(f"cannot read the handoff {handoff}: {e}") from None
    if not todos:
        return
    if allow:
        print(f"ATTENTION: --allow-todo: {len(todos)} TODO line(s) in § 0–2 of {handoff} stay open — the successor "
              f"will rebuild that state from the journal:\n{todo_report(todos)}", file=sys.stderr)
        return
    raise hc.UsageError(f"{handoff}: § 0–2 still hold {len(todos)} TODO line(s) — the successor starts from them, so "
                        f"fill them in (or pass --allow-todo):\n{todo_report(todos)}")


def find_local_by_cli(cli_sid: str):
    """Desktop metadata of the session with this cli id; an id shorter than a uuid is a prefix and
    must match exactly one session (an ambiguous prefix is an error, not a guess)."""
    prefix = len(cli_sid) < 36
    hits = []
    for path in hc.sessions_dir().glob("*/*/local_*.json"):
        try:
            meta = json.loads(path.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            continue
        c = meta.get("cliSessionId") or ""
        if c == cli_sid or (prefix and c.startswith(cli_sid)):
            hits.append(meta)
    if len(hits) > 1:
        raise hc.Failure(f"prefix {cli_sid!r} matches {len(hits)} sessions "
                         f"({', '.join(h.get('sessionId', '?') for h in hits[:4])}) — write the full id")
    return hits[0] if hits else None


def session_by_any(sid: str) -> dict:
    """{'local','cli','name'} for a local_… id, a full cli uuid or an 8-char cli prefix; empty fields when unknown."""
    sid = (sid or "").strip().split()[0] if (sid or "").strip() else ""
    if not sid:
        return {"local": "", "cli": "", "name": ""}
    if sid.startswith("local_"):
        meta = hc.desktop_session(sid) or {}
        return {"local": sid, "cli": meta.get("cliSessionId", ""), "name": meta.get("title", "")}
    meta = find_local_by_cli(sid) or {}
    return {"local": meta.get("sessionId", ""), "cli": meta.get("cliSessionId") or sid, "name": meta.get("title", "")}


def hub_candidates(stage: str, exclude: tuple = ()) -> dict:
    """Who was hub before, by source: roles `hub`, night-queue `coordinator:`.

    Sessions in `exclude` (the new hub, as local and cli id) are dropped, so a re-run after a
    partial takeover still finds the real predecessor in whichever file was not yet rewritten.
    """
    out = {}
    rec = hc.roles_load(stage)["roles"].get("hub")
    if rec:
        out["roles"] = {"local": rec.get("session", "") if str(rec.get("session", "")).startswith("local_") else "",
                        "cli": rec.get("cli_session_id", ""), "name": rec.get("title", ""), "tag": rec.get("tag", "")}
    q = nightq_read(stage)
    if q and q.get("coordinator"):
        out["night-queue"] = dict(session_by_any(q["coordinator"]), tag="")
    return {k: v for k, v in out.items()
            if v.get("cli") or v.get("local")
            if not ({v.get("local"), v.get("cli")} & set(x for x in exclude if x))}


def previous_hub(stage: str, exclude: tuple = ()) -> dict:
    """{'local','cli','name','tag'} of the hub being replaced: roles, else night-queue."""
    c = hub_candidates(stage, exclude)
    for src in ("roles", "night-queue"):
        if src in c:
            return c[src]
    return {"local": "", "cli": "", "name": "", "tag": ""}


def registry_of(sid: str):
    """([(stage, role, record, live)], complete): every record of the session `sid` in the registry of any stage — live
    roles and retired ones, so an earlier hub still counts. `complete` is False when some registry could not be read
    (the answer may be missing a record)."""
    if not sid:
        return [], True
    try:
        names = sorted(d.name for d in hc.root().iterdir() if (d / "roles.json").is_file())
    except OSError:
        return [], False
    hits, complete = [], True
    for name in names:
        try:
            data = hc.roles_load(name)
            roles = [(role, rec, True) for role, rec in data["roles"].items()]
            roles += [(rec.get("role"), rec, False) for rec in data["retired"]]
            hits += [(name, role, rec, live) for role, rec, live in roles if sid in (rec.get("session"), rec.get("cli_session_id"))]
        except (hc.Failure, hc.UsageError, OSError, ValueError, AttributeError, TypeError):
            complete = False
    return hits, complete


def holder_of(sid: str):
    """(stage, record, is_hub) of the hub or agent a lock belongs to; (None, None, False) when that cannot be told
    for sure. A live role beats a retired record (a hub retired in stage A and live in stage B belongs to B); more
    than one stage, or a registry that could not be read, is not told. is_hub: the record is the `hub` role, live or
    retired."""
    hits, complete = registry_of(sid)
    pool = [h for h in hits if h[3]] or hits
    stages = {h[0] for h in pool}
    if not complete or len(stages) != 1:
        return None, None, False
    return pool[0][0], pool[0][2], all(h[1] == "hub" for h in pool)


def holder_activity(stage, rec) -> str:
    """How long ago the lock holder's stage journal last heard from it: the latest line signed with its tag."""
    tag = (rec or {}).get("tag") or (rec or {}).get("role")
    if not (stage and tag):
        return "no journal line"
    last = hc.last_line_by_tag(stage, tag, days=7)
    return f"its latest journal line is {hc.age(last)} old" if last else "no journal line in the last 7 days"


def nightq_read(stage: str):
    path = hc.root() / stage / "night-queue.md"
    if not path.exists():
        return None
    return load_script("nightq").read_queue(stage)


def nightq_coordinator(stage: str) -> str:
    """First token of `coordinator:` (the rest of the line may be a comment)."""
    q = nightq_read(stage) or {}
    return (q.get("coordinator") or "").split()[0] if (q.get("coordinator") or "").strip() else ""


def run_step(path: Path, mode: str, env: dict, must_pass: bool = False):
    """A config layer's takeover.sh: `check` exits 0 when its target state is there (or there is nothing to do),
    1 when `apply` is needed; anything else, or a failed `apply`, stops the takeover. Output is shown indented."""
    try:
        res = subprocess.run([str(path), mode], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=120, env=hc.child_env(env))
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
        raise hc.Failure(f"{path} {mode} did not finish in 120 s") from None
    for line in (res.stdout + res.stderr).strip().splitlines()[-8:]:
        print(f"    {line}")
    if mode == "check" and res.returncode in (0, 1):
        return None if res.returncode == 0 else f"{path.name} check: not done yet"
    if res.returncode != 0:
        raise hc.Failure(f"{path} {mode} exited {res.returncode}")
    return None


def run_tool(argv: list, extra_env=None) -> subprocess.CompletedProcess:
    return subprocess.run([sys.executable, str(hc.BIN / argv[0])] + argv[1:], capture_output=True, text=True,
                          env=hc.child_env(extra_env))


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- digest parts

def pending_line(ask, entries: list) -> str:
    """The one line about owner answers nobody has marked `ask done` (same rule as `ask list --pending`).
    First line of the register block, so `cut` never drops it."""
    ids = [e.id for e in ask.pending_entries(entries)]
    if not ids:
        return "awaiting execution: 0"
    return f"awaiting execution: {len(ids)} ({', '.join(ids[:12])}{', …' if len(ids) > 12 else ''})"


def ask_digest(stage: str, days: int = 1, width: int = 60) -> str:
    """"awaiting execution: N (ids)", then open questions, the owner's recent answers, the agents' decisions in
    force and withdrawals; newest first inside each group, entries with the same text merged into one line."""
    try:
        ask = ask_module()
        _, entries = ask.load(stage)
    except (OSError, SystemExit) as e:
        return f"register unreadable: {e}"
    return pending_line(ask, entries) + "\n" + _ask_digest_groups(ask, entries, days, width)


def _ask_digest_groups(ask, entries: list, days: int, width: int) -> str:
    cutoff = (hc.now().date() - dt.timedelta(days=days)).isoformat()
    groups: dict = {}
    for e in entries:
        m = ask.STAMP_RE.search(e.status)   # the status ends "(YYYY-MM-DD)" or "(YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM)"
        asked = re.match(r"\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}", e.fields.get("asked", ""))
        when = max(asked.group(0) if asked else "", m.group(1) if m else "")
        body = e.status.split(":", 1)[1].strip() if ":" in e.status else ""
        if e.kind_letter == "Q" and e.state in ("open", "default-taken"):
            key = (0, f"{e.state}: {e.title[:width]}")
        elif when < cutoff:
            continue
        elif e.state == "answered":
            key = (1, f"owner: {body[:width]}")
        elif e.kind_letter == "D" and e.state in ("standing", "open"):
            key = (2, f"in force: {e.title[:width]}")
        elif e.state == "withdrawn":
            key = (3, f"withdrawn: {e.title[:width]}")
        else:
            continue
        ids, latest_when = groups.get(key, ([], ""))
        groups[key] = (ids + [e.id], max(latest_when, when))
    if not groups:
        return f"no open entries; no answers or decisions since {cutoff}"
    ordered = sorted(groups.items(), key=lambda kv: (kv[0][0], -int(kv[1][1].replace("-", "") or 0)))
    return "\n".join(f"{', '.join(ids)} {text}" for (_, text), (ids, _) in ordered)


def permissions_digest(stage: str) -> str:
    """Standing permissions in force for the stage and its repository, recorded in any stage (`ask allow --list`)."""
    try:
        return ask_module().permissions_digest(stage)
    except (OSError, SystemExit) as e:
        return f"Standing permissions: register unreadable: {e}"


def locks_digest() -> str:
    b = board_module()
    try:
        locks = [r for r in b.load() if b.is_active(r)]
    except b.BoardError as e:
        return f"board is broken: {e}"
    if not locks:
        return "no active locks"
    return "\n".join(f"{r['kind']} ({r.get('repo') or b.DEFAULT_REPO}) — {r.get('owner_name')} until "
                     f"{r['until'][5:16].replace('T', ' ')}" for r in locks)


def roles_digest(stage: str) -> str:
    data = hc.roles_load(stage)
    if not data["roles"]:
        return "registry is empty"
    rows = []
    for name, rec in sorted(data["roles"].items()):
        last = hc.last_line_by_tag(stage, rec.get("tag") or name)
        rows.append(f"{name} [{rec.get('tag')}] {rec['kind']} {rec['session']} — journal {hc.age(last)} ago")
    return "\n".join(rows)


def jwait_command(stage: str, tag: str, since=None) -> str:
    since_opt = f"--since {since:%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M} " if since else ""
    return (f"jwait --journal --stage {stage} --tag {tag} --tag hub --hub-events "
            f"{since_opt}--for {hc.jwait_for()} --note \"scheduled round\"")


def hub_notes_line(stage: str) -> str:
    """Pointers to the project's hub rules (hub-rules.md: overrides of the skill's recommended rules, every layer)
    and hub notes (HUB-NOTES.md, the first layer's), read before planning."""
    out = []
    rules = [d / "hub-rules.md" for d in reversed(hc.config_dirs(stage)) if (d / "hub-rules.md").is_file()]
    if rules:
        out.append("Hub rules that override the skill's defaults — read before planning (later wins): "
                   + ", ".join(map(str, rules)))
    notes = hc.config_file("HUB-NOTES.md", stage)
    if notes:
        out.append(f"Hub notes of this project — read before planning: {notes}")
    return "\n".join(out)


def wait_procedure() -> str:
    """Wait advice for the host writing this digest or handoff."""
    if hc.host_engine() == "codex":
        return "Codex: use a yielded shell session and its continuation tool; keep each wait at most 60 s"
    return "Claude: Bash `run_in_background: true`"


def watchdog_digest(stage: str) -> str:
    """What the watchdog does for this stage, for the takeover digest: an active do-not-wake marker, and that the job
    is on. Empty when the watchdog is off and nothing is paused. Never fails the takeover."""
    try:
        wd = load_script("watchdog")
        return "\n".join(x for x in (wd.marker_line(stage), wd.status_line(stage)) if x)
    except Exception:  # noqa: BLE001
        return ""


def session_host(stage: str, session: str, cli: str, kind: str, engine: str) -> str:
    """Where this hub runs, for the watchdog's choice of how to wake it: `desktop`, `detached` (a headless hub started
    by `agent spawn`), `codex-app` (the current confirmed app thread), `bg` (a `claude --bg` session) or `term`
    (a terminal session); "" when it cannot be told. Creation provenance in a rollout is not the current host."""
    if kind == "desktop":
        return "desktop"
    if engine == "codex":
        if hc.detached(stage, {"session": session, "cli_session_id": cli}, engine="codex"):
            return "detached"
        if (engines.codex_desktop() and UUID_RE.fullmatch(cli or "")
                and session == cli == os.environ.get("CODEX_THREAD_ID", "").strip()):
            return "codex-app"
        return ""
    if hc.detached(stage, {"session": session, "cli_session_id": cli}):
        return "detached"
    for path in (session_effort.claude_home() / "sessions").glob("*.json"):
        try:
            rec = json.loads(path.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            continue
        if isinstance(rec, dict) and cli and rec.get("sessionId") == cli:
            return {"bg": "bg", "background": "bg", "interactive": "term"}.get(str(rec.get("kind")), "")
    return ""


def pace_digest(stage: str) -> str:
    """The limit-pace advisor line of each engine (bin/limit_pace.py), for the digest. Never fails the takeover."""
    try:
        import limit_pace
        if limit_pace.mode() == "off":
            return ""
        paces = limit_pace.read_all()
        return "Limit pace (choose this launch: agent spawn --dry-run):\n" + "\n".join(
            limit_pace.compact(e, paces, stage) for e in limit_pace.ENGINES)
    except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001 — the line says it is missing and why, so a broken advisor is not silent
        return f"Limit pace: unavailable ({type(e).__name__})"


def digest(stage: str, n: int, name: str, handoff: Path, steps: list, notes: list = (), warns: list = (),
           goal: str = "") -> str:
    tag = f"hub-{n}"
    # the first jwait replays everything since the predecessor wrote the handoff
    since = dt.datetime.fromtimestamp(handoff.stat().st_mtime, hc.TZ) if handoff else None
    text = handoff.read_text(encoding="utf-8") if handoff else ""
    parts = [
        (f"DIGEST \"{name}\": " + "; ".join(steps), 300, ""),
        (hc.plugin_runtime_line(), 650, ""),
        (hc.DESKTOP_CARDS_LINE if hc.host_engine() != "codex" else "", 200, ""),
        (f"Goal of stage {stage}: {goal}" if goal else "", 300, ""),
        ("ATTENTION:\n" + "\n".join(notes) if notes else "", 500, ""),
        ("\n".join(f"ATTENTION: {w}" for w in warns), 900, ""),
        (hub_notes_line(stage), 300, ""),
        (watchdog_digest(stage), 400, "watchdog status"),
        (pace_digest(stage), 480, "agent-top --once"),
        (f"First jwait ({wait_procedure()}; --since = handoff time):\n"
         + jwait_command(stage, tag, since), 600, ""),
        (f"§ 0 of the handoff {handoff.name if handoff else '—'}:\n" + (section(text, 0) or "(no § 0)"), 1100,
         str(handoff) if handoff else ""),
        # after § 0 and its handoff pointer, which keep their budget; the block fits itself into ~520 bytes (what does
        # not fit is "K more: ask allow --list"), so the register after it still gets most of the rest
        (permissions_digest(stage), 600, f"ask allow --list --stage {stage}"),
        ("ask register (check every \"owner said\" of the handoff against it; on a mismatch the register wins — "
         "ask the owner):\n" + ask_digest(stage), 1300, f"ask list --stage {stage}"),
        ("Locks:\n" + locks_digest(), 380, "lock list"),
        ("Roles:\n" + roles_digest(stage), 360, "roles list"),
    ]
    out = "\n\n".join(cut(t, lim, where) for t, lim, where in parts if t)
    return cut(out, DIGEST_BYTES)


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the replaced hub that still runs

def running_session(cli_id: str):
    """The `claude agents --json` row of a session that still runs (it has a pid, or reports a live status — a `done`
    background session that keeps its pid still accepts messages), else None. Bounded and silent: any failure of the
    CLI is None, never an error."""
    if not cli_id:
        return None
    try:
        cli = hc.find_claude(persist=False)
        if cli is None:
            return None
        res = subprocess.run([cli.path, "agents", "--json"], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=10,
                             env=autopilot.child_env(), stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL)
        rows = json.loads(res.stdout)
    except (hc.Failure, OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError, ValueError):
        return None
    for r in rows if isinstance(rows, list) else []:
        if not isinstance(r, dict) or cli_id not in (r.get("sessionId"), r.get("id")):
            continue
        if r.get("pid") or (r.get("state") != "done" and r.get("status") in ("busy", "idle", "waiting", "running")):
            return r
    return None


def stop_background(row: dict, cli_id: str) -> str:
    """`claude stop <id>` for a background session (bounded; its history stays, nothing is removed): "" when it was
    stopped, else why not. Never raises."""
    rid = row.get("id") or cli_id
    try:
        cli = hc.find_claude(persist=False)
        if cli is None:
            return "the claude CLI was not found"
        res = subprocess.run([cli.path, "stop", rid], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=20,
                             env=autopilot.child_env(), stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL)
    except (hc.Failure, OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError) as e:
        return str(e) or type(e).__name__
    return "" if res.returncode == 0 else f"`claude stop {rid}` exited {res.returncode}"


def replaced_hub(prev: dict, new_session: str, new_cli: str, stage: str, dry_run: bool = False,
                 label: str = "the previous hub") -> tuple:
    """(stopped, warning) about the hub registered before this takeover (`prev`, its roles record) when it still runs
    — otherwise ("", ""): other hubs find it by name (ListAgents) and message it instead of the registered hub.
    A background session that is not busy is stopped (`claude stop`, history kept; `stopped` says so). A busy one, a
    Desktop session, a terminal session, the session running this command and a stop that failed are left alone and
    named in the warning with how to stop them. A failing CLI is silent."""
    if not prev or ({prev.get("session"), prev.get("cli_session_id")} - {None, ""}) & {new_session, new_cli}:
        return "", ""
    import codex_sessions
    if prev.get("engine") == "codex" or codex_sessions.detached(stage, prev):
        return "", codex_sessions.previous_warning(stage, prev)  # a Codex hub: named, never stopped from here
    desktop = str(prev.get("session") or "").startswith("local_")
    cli_id = prev.get("cli_session_id") or ("" if desktop else str(prev.get("session") or ""))
    row = running_session(cli_id)
    if row is None:
        return "", ""
    who = f"\"{prev.get('title') or row.get('name') or prev.get('tag') or '?'}\" ({prev.get('tag') or 'hub'}, sid {cli_id[:8]}"
    who += f", pid {row['pid']})" if row.get("pid") else ")"
    rid = row.get("id") or cli_id
    by_name = f"{label} {who} still runs: other hubs can still message it by name and it answers"
    if desktop:
        return "", f"{by_name} — archive it in Desktop ({prev['session']}); a Desktop hub archives it itself with mcp__ccd_session_mgmt__archive_session. Nothing was stopped."
    if row.get("kind") != "background":
        return "", f"{by_name} — close its terminal session. Nothing was stopped."
    own = hc.session_id()
    if own and own in (row.get("sessionId"), row.get("id"), cli_id):
        return "", f"{by_name} — it is the session running this command, so it was not stopped."
    if row.get("status") == "busy":
        return "", (f"{by_name} — it is working now (status busy), so it was not stopped: `claude stop {rid}` once it is "
                    "idle (`claude rm` would delete its history).")
    if dry_run:
        return f"[plan] stop {label} {who}: `claude stop {rid}`", ""
    failed = stop_background(row, cli_id)
    if failed:
        return "", f"{by_name} — stopping it failed ({failed}): `claude stop {rid}` by hand. Nothing was stopped."
    return f"stopped {label} {who} (`claude stop {rid}`; its history stays, `claude attach {rid}` shows it)", ""


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- takeover steps

class Plan:
    def __init__(self, dry: bool):
        self.dry = dry
        self.done: list = []

    def step(self, title: str, do, verify, short: str = "") -> None:
        """do() then verify(); verify() returning None before do() means the step is already done."""
        short = short or title
        if verify() is None:
            self.done.append(f"{short} (already)")
            print(f"[already done] {title}")
            return
        if self.dry:
            self.done.append(f"{short} — planned")
            print(f"[plan] {title}")
            return
        try:
            do()
        except hc.Failure:
            raise
        except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001 — any error stops the takeover with its step name
            raise hc.Failure(f"step \"{title}\" failed: {e}") from None
        problem = verify()
        if problem:
            raise hc.Failure(f"step \"{title}\" did not verify: {problem}. The following steps were not run.")
        self.done.append(f"{short} ✓")
        print(f"[ok] {title}")


def edit_nightq(stage: str, coordinator: str, updated: str) -> None:
    path = hc.root() / stage / "night-queue.md"
    lines = path.read_text(encoding="utf-8").splitlines(keepends=True)
    seen = set()
    for i, line in enumerate(lines):
        for key, value in (("coordinator", coordinator), ("updated", updated)):
            if key not in seen and line.startswith(f"{key}:"):
                lines[i] = f"{key}: {value}\n"
                seen.add(key)
    if "coordinator" not in seen:
        raise hc.Failure(f"{path} has no coordinator: line")
    if "updated" not in seen:
        idx = next(i for i, ln in enumerate(lines) if ln.startswith("coordinator:"))
        lines.insert(idx + 1, f"updated: {updated}\n")
    hc.atomic_write(path, "".join(lines))


def start_line_present(stage: str, tag: str, session: str) -> bool:
    try:
        lines = hc.journal_path(stage).read_text(encoding="utf-8").splitlines()
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return False
    for line in lines:
        p = hc.parse_journal_line(line)
        if p and p[1] == tag and p[2].startswith("start:") and session in p[2]:
            return True
    return False


def new_hub_session(raw: str) -> tuple:
    """(session id to record, cli id, kind, desktop title) of the new hub."""
    raw = raw.strip()
    if raw.startswith("local_") or not UUID_RE.fullmatch(raw):
        local = hc.normalize_local_id(raw)
        meta = hc.desktop_session(local)
        if meta is None:
            raise hc.Failure(f"session {local} not found in {hc.sessions_dir()} (a full local_… id, or a CLI "
                             "session uuid, is required)")
        if meta.get("isArchived"):
            raise hc.Failure(f"session {local} is archived")
        cli = meta.get("cliSessionId") or ""
        if not cli:
            raise hc.Failure(f"session {local} has no cliSessionId — no id to record the locks on")
        return local, cli, "desktop", meta.get("title") or ""
    # a bare uuid: a Desktop session id without the local_ prefix, its CLI id, or a terminal Claude Code session
    if hc.desktop_session(raw) is not None:
        return new_hub_session(hc.normalize_local_id(raw))
    meta = find_local_by_cli(raw)
    if meta:
        return meta.get("sessionId"), raw, "desktop", meta.get("title") or ""
    return raw, raw, "cli", ""


def environment_warnings(persist: bool = True) -> list:
    """Why agents started from here would misbehave, one line each: a Claude Code CLI older than hc.MIN_CLI_VERSION
    (its aliases resolve to older models), a same-named command earlier on PATH than the plugin's tools, a hub home in
    the legacy ~/.claude/agent-hub (protected by Claude Code). Never fails:
    a lookup that does not work is no warning."""
    out = []
    try:
        out.append(hc.cli_warning(hc.find_claude(persist=persist)))
    except hc.Failure:
        pass
    out.append(hc.shadow_warning(hc.shadowed_tools()))
    h = hc.home()
    if h.layer == "legacy":
        out.append(f"the hub home is the legacy {h.path}, under ~/.claude, which Claude Code protects (every edit there "
                   f"asks or is refused, the Bash sandbox refuses writes): `hub home migrate` moves it to {hc.user_home()}")
    return [w for w in out if w]


def resolve_self(raw: str) -> str:
    """`--session self` = the current Claude or Codex host, including detached workers."""
    if raw.strip() != "self":
        return raw
    sid = hc.session_id() or os.environ.get("AGENT_SESSION_ID", "").strip()
    if not sid:
        raise hc.UsageError("--session self: neither $CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID nor $CODEX_THREAD_ID nor $AGENT_SESSION_ID (set by `agent spawn`) "
                            "is set here — pass the full session id")
    return sid


PATH_OPTIONS = ("--repo", "--handoff")


def absolute_argv(argv: list) -> list:
    """`argv` with the values of the path options made absolute: the command is repeated from another directory, where a
    relative --repo or --handoff names nothing."""
    out, i = [], 0
    while i < len(argv):
        x = argv[i]
        if x in PATH_OPTIONS and i + 1 < len(argv):
            out += [x, os.path.abspath(os.path.expanduser(argv[i + 1]))]
            i += 2
            continue
        for opt in PATH_OPTIONS:
            if x.startswith(opt + "="):
                x = f"{opt}={os.path.abspath(os.path.expanduser(x[len(opt) + 1:]))}"
        out.append(x)
        i += 1
    return out


def locate(a, stage: str, n: int):
    """The location rule (hc.check_location) for `hub start` and `hub takeover`, once per command: None when the hub may
    go on (a.project, a.location_note say where), else the exit code 4 — the session must move first, nothing has
    been registered, journaled or locked."""
    if hasattr(a, "project"):
        return None
    rerun = " ".join([autopilot.tool("hub")] + [shlex.quote(x) for x in absolute_argv(a.argv)])
    loc = hc.check_location(stage, n, rerun, a.repo, a.no_project, a.dry_run)
    a.project, a.location_note = loc.repo, loc.note
    return loc.code


def check_naming(stage: str, goal, rerun: bool) -> None:
    """`hub start` of a new stage needs a name that carries a word about the work and a goal line (the stage's own, kept
    in stage.json, counts). A re-run by the registered hub is not asked again; AGENT_HUB_NO_NAMING=1 skips both."""
    if rerun or not hc.naming_enforced():
        return
    if (problem := hc.stage_name_problem(stage)) is not None:
        raise hc.UsageError(problem)
    if not hc.clean_goal(goal) and not hc.stage_goal(stage):
        raise hc.UsageError("hub start needs --goal \"<one line: what the stage delivers, in the owner's words>\" — it "
                            "goes into the hub's title, the digest and agent-top")


def cmd_start(a) -> int:
    stage = hc.check_stage(a.stage)
    a.session = resolve_self(a.session)
    n, rec = registered_hub(stage)
    session, cli, _, _ = new_hub_session(a.session)
    if rec and rec.get("session") not in (session, cli) and rec.get("cli_session_id") != cli:
        raise hc.UsageError(f"stage {stage} already has a hub ({rec.get('title') or rec.get('session')}, tag "
                            f"{rec.get('tag')}) — use `hub takeover --stage {stage} --session …`")
    prev = latest("HANDOFF-hub-*.md", stage)
    if prev is not None and not rec:
        raise hc.UsageError(f"stage {stage} has a handoff ({prev.name}) — use `hub takeover --stage {stage} --session …`")
    check_naming(stage, a.goal, rerun=bool(rec))
    a.n = a.n or n or closed_next(stage) or 1
    pending = autopilot.load_state(stage).get('pending') or {}
    if native_refresh_candidate(pending, rec or {}, session, a.n):
        # Route before start's location/project work. Recheck the exact token under the mutex,
        # even if another takeover removes/replaces the pending record before we acquire it.
        a.desktop_refresh_request = pending['request_id']
        a.handoff, a.start, a.auto_handoff = None, True, False
        return cmd_takeover(a)
    if (code := locate(a, stage, a.n)) is not None:
        return code
    if not a.dry_run:
        hc.work_dir(stage).mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    a.handoff, a.start, a.auto_handoff = None, True, False
    for warning in environment_warnings(persist=not a.dry_run):
        print(f"ATTENTION: {warning}")
    return cmd_takeover(a)


def cmd_takeover(a) -> int:
    try:
        return locked_takeover(a)
    except OSError as e:
        if getattr(a, "desktop_request", None):
            raise hc.Failure(f"desktop stage-home access/takeover failed: {e}; takeover is not verified") from None
        raise


def native_refresh_candidate(pending, current, session, n) -> bool:
    """Classify a completed native self-refresh, including its stale original actor, without proving it."""
    return bool(pending.get("surface") == "desktop" and pending.get("taken_over")
                and (n is None or n == pending.get("n"))
                and (session in (pending.get("id"), pending.get("actual_thread_id"))
                     or current.get("session") == session and current.get("surface") == "desktop"))


def native_self_refresh(a, stage, session, request) -> int:
    """Called under the state mutex; proof and completion never enter the generic takeover Plan."""
    # Use parsed actions so argparse abbreviations cannot silently discard a requested operation.
    # main-merge-until has a default, so retain the explicit option check even for that same value.
    explicit_until = any(arg.split("=", 1)[0].startswith("--") and arg.split("=", 1)[0] != "--"
                         and "--main-merge-until".startswith(arg.split("=", 1)[0]) for arg in a.argv)
    if (a.take_main_merge or a.skip_lock or explicit_until or a.goal is not None
            or a.name is not None or a.repo is not None or a.no_project):
        raise hc.UsageError("native self-refresh cannot transfer resources or change metadata/location; "
                            "run an independently authorized resource operation separately")
    with hc.roles_lock(stage):
        _, pending, _ = autopilot.desktop_identity_proof(stage, request, session)
        if getattr(a, "desktop_request", None):
            if not a.auto_handoff:
                raise hc.UsageError("--desktop-request requires --auto-handoff")
            if a.handoff is None or Path(a.handoff).expanduser().resolve() != Path(pending['handoff']).resolve():
                raise hc.Failure("takeover handoff differs from the desktop reservation")
        # The proof requires this exact host/cwd already registered. Nothing needs rewriting:
        # no locks, queue, project callbacks, predecessor stop, shift, start line or reservation.
        print(f"Native hub-{pending['n']} self-refresh verified; request and registration retained"
              + (" (dry run)" if a.dry_run else ""))
    return 0


def locked_takeover(a) -> int:
    stage = hc.check_stage(a.stage)
    if not (hc.root() / stage).is_dir() and not (getattr(a, "start", False) and a.dry_run):
        raise hc.UsageError(f"no stage directory {hc.root() / stage} — the first hub of a stage runs "
                            f'`hub start --stage {stage} --goal "<what the stage delivers>" --session <your session id>`')
    # Serialize role migration with launch/bind and other takeovers. Desktop validation precedes locks/roles/journal.
    with contextlib.nullcontext() if a.dry_run else autopilot.state_lock(hc.check_stage(a.stage)):
        request = getattr(a, "desktop_request", None)
        pending = autopilot.load_state(a.stage).get("pending") or {}
        if a.auto_handoff and pending.get("surface") == "desktop" and not request:
            raise hc.UsageError("desktop automatic takeover requires --desktop-request from its brief")
        session = resolve_self(a.session)
        current = hc.roles_load(stage)['roles'].get('hub') or {}
        expected_refresh = getattr(a, "desktop_refresh_request", None)
        if expected_refresh or native_refresh_candidate(pending, current, session, a.n):
            with autopilot.state_lock(stage) if a.dry_run else contextlib.nullcontext():
                return native_self_refresh(a, stage, session, expected_refresh or request or pending['request_id'])
        if request:
            if a.n is not None and a.n != pending.get("n"):
                raise hc.UsageError("desktop takeover number must match the reserved successor")
            if not a.auto_handoff:
                raise hc.UsageError("--desktop-request requires --auto-handoff")
            if not a.dry_run:
                autopilot.desktop_preflight(a.stage, request, resolve_self(a.session), a.handoff)
    return _cmd_takeover(a)


def _cmd_takeover(a) -> int:
    stage = hc.check_stage(a.stage)
    starting = getattr(a, "start", False)
    if not (hc.root() / stage).is_dir() and not (starting and a.dry_run):
        raise hc.UsageError(f"no stage directory {hc.root() / stage} — the first hub of a stage runs "
                            f"`hub start --stage {stage} --goal \"<what the stage delivers>\" --session <your session id>`")
    a.session = resolve_self(a.session)
    session, cli, kind, title = new_hub_session(a.session)
    handoff = Path(a.handoff).expanduser() if a.handoff else (None if starting else latest("HANDOFF-hub-*.md", stage))
    grill = grilling.active_stage(stage) if a.auto_handoff and not starting else None
    if (grill and grill.get("session") not in (session, cli)
            and not grilling.owner_asked_for(grill, autopilot.load_state(stage).get("pending") or {}, handoff)):
        # a successor started before the hub began grilling the owner: it waits until the grilling ends
        raise hc.UsageError(f"takeover: the hub of stage {stage} is grilling the owner (since "
                            f"{str(grill.get('since'))[11:16]}): an automatic takeover waits until it ends "
                            f"(`hub grilling end`) or the owner asks for the handoff — then run this command again")
    env_sid = hc.session_id()
    if env_sid and env_sid != cli:
        print(f"ATTENTION: not run from session {session} (your sid {env_sid[:8]}, its sid {cli[:8]}); "
              "the locks are recorded on it", file=sys.stderr)
    if handoff is not None and not handoff.is_file():
        raise hc.UsageError(f"--handoff {handoff}: no such file")
    notes = []
    # the successor `hub succeed` started takes the number it was started under (its name, the jwait it is awaited by)
    n = (a.n or (autopilot.pending_number(stage, handoff) if a.auto_handoff else None)
         or takeover_number(stage, session, cli, handoff, notes))
    tag = f"hub-{n}"
    goal = hc.clean_goal(a.goal) or hc.stage_goal(stage)  # takeover never refuses on the name; --goal sets or replaces it
    name = a.name or hc.hub_title(stage, n, goal)
    if (code := locate(a, stage, n)) is not None:
        return code
    if not a.dry_run:
        hc.record_stage_goal(stage, goal)

    # Predecessor: every source that does not already name the new hub. A re-run after a partial
    # takeover therefore still finds it, and a stale registry does not hide the real one's locks.
    cands = hub_candidates(stage, exclude=(session, cli))
    prev = previous_hub(stage, exclude=(session, cli))
    owners = {c["cli"] for c in cands.values() if c.get("cli")}
    if len({c.get("cli") for c in cands.values()}) > 1:
        notes.append("sources disagree on the previous hub: " + "; ".join(
            f"{src} → {c.get('name') or '?'} {c.get('local') or c.get('cli')}" for src, c in cands.items())
            + " — taking the locks of all of them")
    for src, c in cands.items():
        if c.get("cli") and len(c["cli"]) < 36:
            notes.append(f"{src}: no session found for the prefix {c['cli']} — its locks were not taken, check `lock list`")
    first = starting or (not cands and handoff is None)
    prev_label = prev["name"] or (prev["local"] or prev["cli"][:8] or ("nobody (first hub of the stage)" if first
                                                                       else "unknown hub"))
    # the registered hub has this very number: the same shift taken again (a restart, a replacement), not a handover
    retake = ""
    if not first and prev.get("tag") and hc.hub_number(prev["tag"]) == n:
        by, _ = handoff_numbers(handoff) if handoff else (None, None)
        retake = (f"re-took shift #{n} (replaces {(prev['cli'] or prev['local'] or '?')[:8]})"
                  + (f", handoff by #{by}" if by else ""))
    t = hc.now()
    b = board_module()
    try:
        active = [r for r in b.load() if b.is_active(r)]
    except b.BoardError as e:
        raise hc.Failure(f"lock board is broken: {e}") from None

    def repo_of(r):
        return r.get("repo") or b.DEFAULT_REPO

    skip = set(a.skip_lock or [])
    explicit_mm = a.take_main_merge
    take_mm = explicit_mm or hc.truthy(hc.setting("AGENT_HUB_TAKE_MAIN_MERGE"))
    # A predecessor's main-merge goes with it only when this stage's record of that session is role hub and the registry
    # was read completely and shows it live nowhere else (the resolver of a third party's lock); any other lock of it
    # is taken as before. What is not taken is looked at below like any foreign lock.
    unsure = {sid for sid in owners if any(r.get("session_id") == sid and r["kind"] == "main-merge" for r in active)
              and holder_of(sid)[::2] != (stage, True)}
    to_take = [r for r in active if r.get("session_id") in owners and r["kind"] not in skip
               and not (r["kind"] == "main-merge" and r.get("session_id") in unsure)]
    kept = [r for r in active if r.get("session_id") in owners and r["kind"] in skip]
    mine = [r for r in active if r.get("session_id") == cli]
    if "main-merge" not in skip:
        # Every main-merge lock is looked at, one per repo. The hub's repo (AGENT_HUB_DEFAULT_REPO; "*" = all) is the
        # only one that can be taken, and only on an explicit --take-main-merge, or, with AGENT_HUB_TAKE_MAIN_MERGE=true,
        # when the holder is an earlier `hub` of this very stage (a takeover) or nobody holds it; the rest is reported and
        # left alone. The config flag never takes a lock from another stage's hub, from an agent of this stage (a merge
        # steward) or from a holder it cannot place, and never on `start`.
        mm_repo = hc.default_repo() or b.DEFAULT_REPO
        mm_configured = bool(hc.setting("AGENT_HUB_DEFAULT_REPO"))  # the nudge below is for a repository that opted in
        ours = {repo_of(r) for r in to_take + mine if r["kind"] == "main-merge"}
        if take_mm and mm_repo == "*":
            notes.append(f"no repository and no AGENT_HUB_DEFAULT_REPO here ({os.getcwd()}): main-merge is looked at for every repo")
        third = [r for r in active if r["kind"] == "main-merge" and repo_of(r) not in ours
                 and (r.get("session_id") not in owners or r.get("session_id") in unsure) and r.get("session_id") != cli]
        for mm in third:
            holder_stage, holder_rec, is_hub = holder_of(mm.get("session_id") or "")
            same_stage = holder_stage == stage and is_hub and not starting
            in_repo = mm_repo == "*" or repo_of(mm) in (mm_repo, "*")
            if in_repo and (explicit_mm or (take_mm and same_stage)):
                to_take.append({"kind": "main-merge", "repo": repo_of(mm), "until": mm["until"],
                                "why": mm.get("why") or "stage hub", "_from": mm.get("owner_name")})
                if explicit_mm:
                    notes.append(f"main-merge ({repo_of(mm)}) is taken from {mm.get('owner_name')} "
                                 f"[{(mm.get('session_id') or '-')[:8]}] of stage {holder_stage or 'unknown'}: "
                                 f"{holder_activity(holder_stage, holder_rec)}")
            else:
                notes.append(f"main-merge ({repo_of(mm)}) is held by {mm.get('owner_name')} "
                             f"[{(mm.get('session_id') or '-')[:8]}] until {mm['until'][:16]}: "
                             f"{(mm.get('why') or '')[:60]} — left alone; take it with --take-main-merge")
        # The hub repo's free main-merge. Never when a main-merge is already ours (taken over from the previous
        # hub or held): a second record, and a wildcard one above all, would lock merges in other repositories.
        held_here = any(repo_of(r) in (mm_repo, "*") for r in active if r["kind"] == "main-merge")
        ours_here = mm_repo in ours or "*" in ours
        any_mm = any(r["kind"] == "main-merge" for r in active)
        if take_mm and not ours_here and not held_here and not (mm_repo == "*" and any_mm):
            to_take.append({"kind": "main-merge", "repo": mm_repo, "until": a.main_merge_until,
                            "why": "stage hub", "_from": None})
        elif not ours_here and not held_here:
            if take_mm:
                notes.append(f"main-merge ({mm_repo}) was wanted but not taken: other main-merge locks exist and the "
                             "hub repo is unknown here — run from the repository or set AGENT_HUB_DEFAULT_REPO")
            elif mm_configured:
                notes.append(f"nobody holds main-merge ({mm_repo}): merges to its main are not guarded — "
                             "--take-main-merge, or AGENT_HUB_TAKE_MAIN_MERGE=true in the repository's config.json")
    if kept:
        notes.append("left with the previous hub (--skip-lock): " + ", ".join(r["kind"] for r in kept))

    warns = []
    todos = open_todos(handoff.read_text(encoding="utf-8")) if handoff else []
    if todos:
        warns.append(f"the handoff {handoff.name} still has {len(todos)} TODO line(s) in § 0–2 (its author did not finish "
                     f"it): rebuild that state from the journal, `ask list` and `lock list` before trusting it — first "
                     f"at line {todos[0][0]}: {todos[0][1][:90]}")
    if engines.selected() != "codex":
        idle = hc.idle_compaction_warning(Path.cwd())
        if idle:
            warns.append(idle)
        if kind == "desktop":
            note = hc.desktop_compaction_note()
            if note:
                warns.append(note)
    plan = Plan(a.dry_run)
    print(f"{name}: {session} (sid {cli[:8]}, {kind}) " + (f"starts stage {stage}" if first else
          (retake.replace("re-took", "re-takes", 1) if retake else f"takes over from \"{prev_label}\"")
          + f"; handoff {handoff or '—'}"))
    for note in notes:
        print(f"ATTENTION: {note}")
    for w in warns:
        print(f"ATTENTION: {w}")
    for r in mine:
        print(f"[already done] lock {r['kind']} ({repo_of(r)}) is yours until {r['until'][:16]}")

    for r in to_take:
        repo = repo_of(r)
        if retake:  # only the last link: a re-taken shift must not nest the earlier takeovers' texts in its reason
            why = f"{name} {session}, {retake}: {peel_why(r.get('why') or '')}".strip()
        else:
            why = f"{name} {session}, took over from {r.get('owner_name') or r.get('_from') or prev_label}: " \
                  f"{r.get('why') or ''}".strip()
        argv = ["lock", "take", r["kind"], "--repo", repo, "--force", "--until", r["until"], "--why", why,
                "--owner-name", name]
        if r.get("value"):
            argv += ["--value", r["value"]]

        def do(argv=argv):
            res = run_tool(argv, {"CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID": cli, "CODEX_THREAD_ID": cli if engines.selected() == "codex" else ""})
            if res.returncode != 0:
                raise hc.Failure(f"lock take {argv[2]}: {res.stderr.strip() or res.stdout.strip()}")

        def verify(kind=r["kind"], repo=repo):
            held = [x for x in b.load() if x["kind"] == kind and (x.get("repo") or b.DEFAULT_REPO) == repo]
            ok = held and held[0].get("session_id") == cli and b.is_active(held[0])
            return None if ok else f"{kind} ({repo}) on the board is not held by {cli[:8]}"

        extra = f", taken from {r['_from']}" if r.get("_from") else ""
        plan.step(f"lock {r['kind']} ({repo}) until {str(r['until'])[:16]}{extra}", do, verify,
                  short=f"lock {r['kind']}")

    updated = f"{t:%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M} {name} ({session}, sid {cli[:8]}) " + (retake or f"took over from {prev_label}") + \
              (f" by {handoff.name}" if handoff else "")
    if nightq_read(stage) is None:
        print("no night-queue.md — step skipped")
    else:
        # the night nudge looks the coordinator up by this value: a Desktop session by its local_ id
        plan.step("night-queue.md: coordinator/updated",
                  lambda: edit_nightq(stage, session, updated),
                  lambda: None if nightq_coordinator(stage) == session else "coordinator: was not written",
                  short="night-queue")

    step = hc.config_file("takeover.sh", stage)
    if step is None:
        print("no takeover.sh in the config layers (" + ", ".join(str(d) for d in hc.config_dirs(stage))
              + f"; cwd {os.getcwd()}) — no project step")
    elif not os.access(step, os.X_OK):
        notes.append(f"{step} is not executable — project takeover step skipped")
        print(f"ATTENTION: {notes[-1]}")
    else:
        step_env = {"HUB_STAGE": stage, "HUB_N": str(n), "HUB_TAG": tag, "HUB_NAME": name, "HUB_SESSION": session,
                    "HUB_CLI_SESSION": cli, "HUB_PREVIOUS": prev_label, "HUB_TAKEOVER_AT": t.isoformat(timespec="minutes"),
                    "HUB_HANDOFF": str(handoff or "")}
        plan.step(f"project step {step}",
                  lambda: run_step(step, "apply", step_env, must_pass=True),
                  lambda: run_step(step, "check", step_env),
                  short="takeover.sh")

    prev_rec = dict(hc.roles_load(stage)["roles"].get("hub") or {})
    roles_cli = load_script("roles")
    # External config steps run outside this mutex; role and chain publication stay serialized.
    with contextlib.nullcontext() if a.dry_run else autopilot.state_lock(stage):
        request = getattr(a, "desktop_request", None)
        if request and not a.dry_run:
            autopilot.desktop_preflight(stage, request, cli, handoff)
        plan.step(f"roles: hub → {session} [{tag}]",
                  lambda: roles_cli.set_role(stage, "hub", session, kind, tag=tag, title=name,
                                             note=f"hub takeover from {prev_label}"),
                  lambda: None if hc.roles_load(stage)["roles"].get("hub", {}).get("session") == session
                  else "role was not recorded",
                  short="roles")
        if not a.dry_run:
            with hc.roles_lock(stage):
                data = hc.roles_load(stage)
                data["roles"]["hub"]["engine"] = engines.selected()
                host = session_host(stage, session, cli, kind, engines.selected())
                if data["roles"]["hub"].get("host") == "codex-app" and host != "codex-app":
                    data["roles"]["hub"].pop("cwd", None)
                if host:
                    data["roles"]["hub"]["host"] = host  # the watchdog's way of waking it (bin/watchdog)
                elif engines.selected() == "codex":
                    data["roles"]["hub"].pop("host", None)
                if host == "codex-app":
                    data["roles"]["hub"]["cwd"] = os.getcwd()
                # where `hub succeed` starts the successor from, whatever directory the hub's shell drifts to later
                top = hc.git_toplevel(os.getcwd()) if getattr(a, "project", None) is not None else None
                if top is not None:
                    data["roles"]["hub"]["worktree"] = str(top)
                else:
                    data["roles"]["hub"].pop("worktree", None)
                if request:
                    pend = autopilot.load_state(stage)["pending"]
                    data["roles"]["hub"].update(surface="desktop", project_id=pend["project_id"],
                                               cwd=pend["cwd"], observed=pend["observed"])
                hc.roles_save(stage, data)
            if request:
                autopilot.desktop_complete(stage, request)
            else:
                autopilot.on_takeover(stage, n, a.auto_handoff, cli, locked=True)

    stopped, live = replaced_hub(prev_rec, session, cli, stage, a.dry_run)
    if stopped:
        print(stopped)
        if not a.dry_run:
            notes.append(stopped)  # the start line and the digest say so too
    if live:
        print(f"ATTENTION: {live}")
        warns.append(live)

    closed = hc.stage_closed(stage)
    if closed:  # `hub close` closed it; a new hub reopens it
        reopened = f"reopened the stage closed {str(closed.get('at') or '?')[:16]} ({closed.get('why') or '—'})"
        print(f"[plan] {reopened}" if a.dry_run else reopened)
        if not a.dry_run:
            hc.record_stage_closed(stage, None)
            notes.append(reopened)

    lock_names = ", ".join(sorted({r["kind"] for r in to_take + mine})) or "none"
    start_text = (f"start: \"{name}\" ({session}, sid {cli[:8]}) "
                  + (f"started stage {stage}" if first else (retake or f"took over from \"{prev_label}\""))
                  + (f" by {handoff.name}" if handoff else "") + f"; locks: {lock_names}; " + ("night-queue, " if nightq_read(stage) is not None else "") + "roles updated"
                  + ("; " + "; ".join(notes) if notes else "") + (f"; {a.location_note}" if a.location_note else ""))
    plan.step("journal: start line",
              lambda: hc.journal_append(stage, tag, start_text),
              lambda: None if start_line_present(stage, tag, session) else "no line in the journal",
              short="journal")

    if not a.dry_run:
        if a.project is not None or a.no_project:
            hc.record_stage_project(stage, a.project)  # the next hub may start outside git
    print()
    print(digest(stage, n, name, handoff, plan.done, notes, warns, goal))
    return 0


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- handoff

def hub_sessions(stage: str, given: str, me: dict) -> list:
    """[(cli session uuid, role record)] whose sub-agents `hub handoff` looks for. With --session, that session only.
    Otherwise the registered hub's (its Claude Code id; a Desktop id is looked up) and, when this command runs inside
    another Claude Code session ($CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID, a uuid), that one too: a registry that names an older
    session must not hide the caller's own sub-agents."""
    if given:
        cli = session_by_any(resolve_self(given))["cli"]
        if not subagents.UUID_RE.fullmatch(cli):
            raise hc.UsageError(f"--session {given!r}: not a session I can find — a CLI uuid, or a local_… id from the "
                                "Desktop session metadata")
        hit = hc.role_for_caller(stage) if given.strip() == "self" else hc.role_for_session(stage, cli)
        return [(cli, hit[1] if hit else {})]
    out = []
    cli = me.get("cli") or (session_by_any(me["local"])["cli"] if me.get("local") else "")
    if subagents.UUID_RE.fullmatch(cli or ""):
        rec = hc.roles_load(stage)["roles"].get("hub") or {}
        out.append((cli, rec if cli in (rec.get("cli_session_id"), rec.get("session")) else {}))
    own = hc.session_id()
    if subagents.UUID_RE.fullmatch(own) and own not in [c for c, _ in out]:
        out.append((own, {}))
    return out


def live_subagents(cli: str, rec: dict) -> list:
    """Sub-agents of `cli` that run or have an unexpired unknown observation. The session that runs this command
    is alive by definition; any other is judged by its process (bin/subagents.py)."""
    if cli == hc.session_id():
        alive = True
    else:
        table = subagents.process_table()
        alive = subagents.parent_alive(rec, cli, table, subagents.live_sessions(table))
    return [s for s in subagents.Finder().of_session(cli, alive, time.time()) if s.unresolved]


def subagent_rows(subs: list, session: str = "") -> list:
    """One line per sub-agent: id, description, age of the last write; `session` (a uuid) prefixes it when more than
    one session is checked."""
    rows = []
    for s in subs:
        last = "no transcript yet" if s.mtime is None else f"last write {hc.age(dt.datetime.fromtimestamp(s.mtime, hc.TZ))} ago"
        rows.append(f"{'[' + session[:8] + '] ' if session else ''}{s.aid}  "
                    f"\"{s.description or s.meta.get('agentType') or 'sub-agent'}\"  "
                    f"{'unknown; ' if s.state == 'unknown' else ''}{last}")
    return rows


def cmd_handoff_finish(a, stage: str) -> int:
    """`hub handoff --finish`: the draft is ready to hand over only when § 0–2 hold no TODO (A-03)."""
    path = Path(a.handoff).expanduser() if a.handoff else latest("HANDOFF-hub-*.md", stage)
    if path is None or not path.is_file():
        raise hc.UsageError(f"no handoff to finish: {path or 'none in ' + str(coordinator_dir(stage))} — write one with "
                            f"`hub handoff --stage {stage}` or pass --handoff PATH")
    check_handoff_todos(path, a.allow_todo)
    rest = len(re.findall(r"\bTODO\b", re.sub(r"<!--.*?-->", "", path.read_text(encoding="utf-8"), flags=re.DOTALL)))
    print(f"handoff ready: {path}" + (f" ({rest} TODO left outside § 0–2)" if rest else ""))
    return 0


def cmd_handoff(a) -> int:
    stage = hc.check_stage(a.stage)
    if a.finish:
        return cmd_handoff_finish(a, stage)
    if a.handoff or a.allow_todo:
        raise hc.UsageError("--handoff and --allow-todo go with --finish")
    grill = grilling.active_stage(stage)
    if grill and autopilot.enabled() and not a.owner_asked and not grill.get("ceiling"):
        raise hc.UsageError(grilling.refusal("handoff", stage, grill))
    n = a.n or handoff_number(stage)
    tag = f"hub-{n}"
    name, succ = hub_name(stage, n), hub_name(stage, n + 1)
    t = hc.now()
    out = Path(a.out).expanduser() if a.out else coordinator_dir(stage) / f"HANDOFF-hub-{stage}-{t:%Y-%m-%d-%H%M}.md"
    if out.exists():
        raise hc.Failure(f"{out} already exists — not overwriting (pass another --out)")
    prev_handoff = latest("HANDOFF-hub-*.md", stage)
    me = previous_hub(stage)  # the hub writing this: roles `hub`, else `coordinator:` of night-queue.md
    live_rows = []
    sessions = hub_sessions(stage, a.session, me)
    if not sessions:
        print("delamain: no hub session known (roles `hub`, or --session): its sub-agents were not checked",
              file=sys.stderr)
    for cli, hub_rec in sessions:
        live_rows += subagent_rows(live_subagents(cli, hub_rec), cli if len(sessions) > 1 else "")
    if live_rows and not a.allow_live_subagents:
        print(f"hub handoff: {len(live_rows)} sub-agent(s) of the hub's session "
              f"{' and '.join(c[:8] for c, _ in sessions)} still running or have unknown process state; the successor "
              "cannot message them:", file=sys.stderr)
        print("".join(f"  {r}\n" for r in live_rows) + "Ways out, for each:\n"
              "  1. wait for it: its completion notice arrives in this session;\n"
              "  2. stop it and re-launch the rest with `agent spawn` (its brief and the partial result);\n"
              "  3. record it as lost: `hub handoff --allow-live-subagents` writes the list into the draft's TODO.\n"
              "Then run `hub handoff` again.", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    live_note = ""
    if live_rows:
        live_note = ("\n- TODO: sub-agents of this session still running at handoff or have unknown process state; the successor cannot "
                     "message them; for each say \"relaunched as `agent spawn` role …\" or \"lost: …\":\n"
                     + "\n".join(f"  - {r}" for r in live_rows[:12]) + (f"\n  - … and {len(live_rows) - 12} more" if len(live_rows) > 12 else ""))
    work = hc.work_dir(stage)
    q = nightq_read(stage)
    b = board_module()
    try:
        held = [r for r in b.load() if b.is_active(r) and me["cli"] and r.get("session_id") == me["cli"]]
    except b.BoardError as e:
        held, _ = [], print(f"lock board is broken: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
    locks_cell = "; ".join(f"{r['kind']} ({r.get('repo') or b.DEFAULT_REPO}) until {r['until'][:16]}"
                           for r in held) or "none"
    agents_cell = "none"
    agents_dir = hc.root() / stage / "agents"
    if agents_dir.is_dir():
        res = run_tool(["agent", "status", "--stage", stage])
        agents_cell = "; ".join(line for line in res.stdout.strip().splitlines()
                                if not line.startswith("Plugin runtime:")) or "none"
    summary = run_tool(["ask", "summary"]).stdout.strip().replace("\n", "; ")
    facts_rows = ("| Environments | TODO what runs where: versions, build ids, pending deploys | TODO |\n"
                  "| Main branch | TODO head; what is merged but not deployed | `git log origin/main` |\n"
                  "| Open PRs | TODO number, head, CI, who drives it | TODO |")
    # prints table rows "| What | State | Where |"; the stage's copy, else the repository's, else the hub home's
    hook = hc.config_file("handoff-facts.sh", stage) or hc.root() / stage / "handoff-facts.sh"
    if hook.is_file() and os.access(hook, os.X_OK):
        try:
            res = subprocess.run([str(hook)], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=180, env=hc.child_env())
            rows = [ln for ln in res.stdout.splitlines() if ln.startswith("| ")]
            if res.returncode == 0 and rows:
                facts_rows = "\n".join(rows)
            else:
                facts_rows += f"\n| handoff-facts.sh | exit {res.returncode}, {len(rows)} rows — fill facts by hand | `{hook}` |"
        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
            facts_rows += f"\n| handoff-facts.sh | did not finish in 180 s — fill facts by hand | `{hook}` |"
    own_lines = []
    try:
        for line in hc.journal_path(stage).read_text(encoding="utf-8").splitlines():
            p = hc.parse_journal_line(line)
            if p and hc.tag_is(p[1], tag):
                own_lines.append(line[:220])
    except FileNotFoundError:
        pass

    def esc(s: str) -> str:
        return s.replace("|", "/").replace("\n", " ")

    me_id = me["local"] or me["cli"] or "TODO session id"
    grill_item = (f"\n5. A grilling with the owner was in progress (since {str(grill.get('since'))[11:16]}): resume it — load "
                  f"the grilling skill, `hub grilling start --stage {stage}`, carry on from what follows. TODO: "
                  + (f"topic «{grill['topic']}» — " if grill.get("topic") else "its topic; ")
                  + "the questions asked with the owner's answers (`ask` ids); the open frontier; the next round."
                  if grill else "")
    goal_line = f"\nGoal of the stage: {hc.stage_goal(stage)}" if hc.stage_goal(stage) else ""
    body = f"""# Handoff "{name}" → "{succ}" — {stage} — {t:%Y-%m-%d %H:%M} — ENTRY POINT

<!-- Draft by `hub handoff` {t:%H:%M}: facts collected by the script, TODO is for the hub. ≤ 12 KB. Delete the role's older handoffs. -->
Replaces `{prev_handoff.name if prev_handoff else '—'}`. Journal: `work/journal-{t:%Y-%m-%d}.md` (tags `[{tag}…]`).
Written by session "{name}" ({me_id}, TODO model).{goal_line}
`work/` = `{work}/`.

**Headline.** TODO: one or two sentences — what matters most right now and whose word is behind it (quote + id in `ask`).

## Business DoD
TODO: brief agreed user/business result and its source (plan, brief or register; hub skill, "Planning a stage").
Carry the result and owner-supplied constraints forward; choose implementation details independently.
Report progress against it with technical evidence separately.

## 0. First steps for the successor
1. Name your session "{succ}"; `hub takeover --stage {stage} --session <your full session id> --handoff {out}` —
   locks ({', '.join(r['kind'] for r in held) or 'none held'}), `coordinator:` in night-queue, `roles set hub`, a journal
   line; it prints a digest and the first `jwait` command. Tell "{name}" once that you took over (`roles budget`).
2. The first `jwait` — use the wait procedure printed in the takeover digest; start no other waiters.
3. Check every "owner said" below against `ask list --stage {stage}` (takeover digest); on a mismatch the register wins.
4. TODO: background processes and script questions waiting for an answer (output file, question marker).{grill_item}

## 1. Where things stand ({t:%H:%M})
| What | State | Where it shows |
|---|---|---|
| Hub locks | {esc(locks_cell)} | `lock list` |
| Headless agents | {esc(agents_cell)[:600]} | `agent status` |
{facts_rows}

## 2. Queue
<!-- Finite snapshot of remaining authorized Business DoD with source/scope and explicit owner boundaries.
     Next ready work first; separate preparation dependencies from publication/merge/stage/production gates.
     Item = action | "done" check | brief stop condition | who (model).
     Wait = exact item | blocker | owner/resource | expected event (ask id when applicable). -->
Codex successor: apply the hub skill's Terminal follow-through; reconcile this snapshot against Business DoD before DONE.
1. TODO

## 3. Night queue
{f"`night-queue.md`: open {q['open']}, next — {q['next'] or '—'}." if q else "Not used (an optional module; delete this section)."}

## 4. Owner questions
`ask summary`: {summary or '—'}.
{cut(ask_digest(stage, width=110), 2600, f"ask list --stage {stage}")}
TODO: questions asked in chat without a record — `ask add` first, then their ids here.

## 5. Risks and loose ends
- TODO: what breaks when nobody watches and how it shows; windows; worktrees to clean up (`git worktree list`;
  finished ones: `git worktree remove <path>`).{live_note}

## 6. Skills for the successor
`hub`; TODO: which other skills the queue in § 2 needs — the successor loads them first.

<!-- Last [{tag}] journal lines (for reference, delete when filling in):
{chr(10).join(own_lines[-6:]) or '—'}
-->
"""
    size = len(body.encode("utf-8"))
    if size > 12 * 1024:
        body = cut(body, 12 * 1024 - 200, "journal and lock/roles/agent status")
    hc.atomic_write(out, body)
    print(f"draft: {out} ({len(body.encode('utf-8'))} bytes); TODO to fill: "
          f"{body.count('TODO')}. Nothing released: the successor takes the locks with `hub takeover`.")
    return 0


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- succeed (autopilot)

def check_caller(stage: str, n: int) -> None:
    """Only the registered hub hands its shift over: a stale hub (its successor already took over) must not start or
    stop a successor in the current hub's name. Judged by $CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID, else $HUB_TAG; a terminal without
    either (the owner by hand) passes."""
    rec = hc.roles_load(stage)["roles"].get("hub") or {}
    sid, tag = hc.session_id(), os.environ.get("HUB_TAG", "").strip()
    if sid and rec and sid not in (rec.get("session"), rec.get("cli_session_id")):
        raise hc.UsageError(f"this session ({sid[:8]}) is not the hub of stage {stage} (hub-{n}: "
                            f"{rec.get('title') or rec.get('session')}) — only the registered hub hands over")
    if tag and not sid and tag not in (f"hub-{n}", rec.get("tag")):
        raise hc.UsageError(f"HUB_TAG {tag} is not the hub of stage {stage} (hub-{n}) — only the registered hub hands over")


def check_replace_caller(stage: str, pend: dict) -> None:
    """`hub succeed --replace` is for the hub that started the successor (the session recorded in the pending record) or
    for the owner at a terminal (neither a session id nor a tag); never for the successor itself, which is the
    registered hub by then."""
    rec = hc.roles_load(stage)["roles"].get("hub") or {}
    sid, tag, author = hc.session_id(), os.environ.get("HUB_TAG", "").strip(), pend.get("author") or ""
    if sid and author and sid != author:
        raise hc.UsageError(f"--replace: only the hub that handed over (session {author[:8]}) or the owner at a terminal may "
                            f"replace its successor; this session is {sid[:8]}")
    if sid and not author and sid in (rec.get("session"), rec.get("cli_session_id")):
        raise hc.UsageError(f"this session ({sid[:8]}) is the registered hub of stage {stage} — the successor cannot replace itself")
    if tag and not sid and tag != f"hub-{(pend.get('n') or 1) - 1}":
        raise hc.UsageError(f"HUB_TAG {tag} is not the hub that handed over (hub-{(pend.get('n') or 1) - 1}) — only it may replace its successor")


def successor_cwd(stage: str, given) -> tuple:
    """(directory, note) the successor is started from: --cwd, else the worktree the registered hub recorded at takeover
    (the hub's shell may have drifted anywhere since), else the stage's recorded project, else the shell's directory. A directory that is outside git or in
    another project than the stage's is refused: a successor there would not be a session of the project."""
    note = ""
    if given:
        cwd = Path(given).expanduser().resolve()
    elif (recorded := hc.registered_worktree(stage)) is not None:
        cwd = recorded.resolve()
        if cwd != Path.cwd().resolve():
            note = f"started from the hub's registered worktree {cwd}, not from the shell's directory {Path.cwd()}"
    elif (project := hc.stage_project(stage)) is not None:  # a hub registered before worktrees were recorded
        cwd = project.resolve()
        if cwd != Path.cwd().resolve():
            note = f"started from the stage's project {cwd}, not from the shell's directory {Path.cwd()}"
    else:
        cwd = Path(os.getcwd()).resolve()
    if cwd.is_dir() and (problem := hc.project_cwd_problem(stage, cwd)):
        raise hc.UsageError(f"--cwd {cwd}: {problem}. A successor hub works in a git worktree of its project, never outside "
                            "git. Run `hub succeed` from the hub's own worktree or pass --cwd <that worktree> (a stage "
                            "that has no repository: hub start/takeover --no-project)")
    return cwd, note


def cmd_succeed(a) -> int:
    stage = hc.check_stage(a.stage)
    if not (hc.root() / stage).is_dir():
        raise hc.UsageError(f"no stage directory {hc.root() / stage}")
    if a.replace and (a.again or a.fallback or a.headless):
        raise hc.UsageError("--replace goes alone (with --force, --handoff, --model…): it starts the successor again the way it was started")
    if not (autopilot.enabled() or a.force or a.dry_run):
        raise hc.UsageError("autopilot is off (AGENT_HUB_AUTO_HANDOFF in the hub home's config.json): a hub starts no "
                            "background session unasked. The owner, at a terminal, may pass --force")
    pend = autopilot.load_state(stage).get("pending") or {}
    # --fallback starts a successor too; --replace swaps one that already took over (the grilling hub is gone by then)
    grill = None if a.replace else grilling.active_stage(stage)
    if grill and autopilot.enabled() and not a.owner_asked:  # the ceiling does not lift it: the owner decides
        raise hc.UsageError(grilling.refusal("succeed", stage, grill))
    if a.fallback or (a.replace and not a.handoff):
        # the handoff the pending successor was started from: the numbers come out as they did then
        handoff = pend.get("handoff")
    elif not a.handoff:
        raise hc.UsageError("--handoff is required (the draft `hub handoff` wrote, TODOs filled)")
    else:
        handoff = Path(a.handoff).expanduser().resolve()
        if not handoff.is_file():
            raise hc.UsageError(f"--handoff {handoff}: no such file")
        if not a.replace:  # a replacement restarts the handoff the first successor was started from
            check_handoff_todos(handoff, a.allow_todo)
    if a.replace:
        cwd, cwd_note = successor_cwd(stage, a.cwd)
        # the registered hub is the successor by now: the numbers come from the record, not from the registry
        succ = pend.get("n")
        if not isinstance(succ, int) or not handoff:
            raise hc.Failure("--replace: no successor of a shift is recorded (auto-handoff.json) — nothing to replace")
        out, _ = handoff_numbers(handoff)
        n = out if out and out < succ else succ - 1
        check_replace_caller(stage, pend)
        if not cwd.is_dir():
            raise hc.UsageError(f"--cwd {cwd}: no such directory")
        return autopilot.succeed(stage, n, Path(handoff), a.model, a.permission_mode, cwd, False, a.dry_run, False,
                                 engine=a.engine, succ=succ, effort_arg=a.effort, replace=True, force=a.force, surface="cli")
    # this hub's number (the handoff's outgoing one wins over a guess) and its successor's, from the function the
    # successor's takeover numbers by
    # `hub succeed` has no --n: the numbers are chosen in the handoff's title (`hub handoff --n N` writes it)
    choose = "write the handoff with `hub handoff --stage {} --n <your number>` and pass it as --handoff".format(stage)
    n, notes = handoff_number(stage, handoff, choose), []
    succ = next_number(stage, handoff, notes, "correct the numbers in the handoff's title to choose")
    if succ <= n:
        notes.append(f"the handoff names #{succ} as the successor of hub-{n} — taking #{n + 1}")
        succ = n + 1
    check_caller(stage, n)
    if a.fallback:  # starts from the root the bg session was started in (pending.cwd): the shell's directory is no matter
        return autopilot.fallback(stage, n, a.why, succ, owner_asked=a.owner_asked)
    cwd, cwd_note = successor_cwd(stage, a.cwd)
    if not cwd.is_dir():
        raise hc.UsageError(f"--cwd {cwd}: no such directory")
    if cwd_note:
        notes.append(cwd_note)
    return autopilot.succeed(stage, n, handoff, a.model, a.permission_mode, cwd, a.headless, a.dry_run, a.again,
                             engine=a.engine, succ=succ, notes=tuple(notes), effort_arg=a.effort, surface=a.surface, branch=a.branch, desktop_worktree=a.desktop_worktree,
                             owner_asked=a.owner_asked)


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- grilling

def cmd_grilling(a) -> int:
    sid = a.session or hc.session_id()
    stage = a.stage or (autopilot.hub_stage_of(sid) if sid else None)
    if not stage:
        raise hc.UsageError("grilling: no stage — pass --stage (this session is not a registered hub)")
    stage = hc.check_stage(stage)
    hubs = grilling.hub_sessions(stage)
    if hubs is None:
        raise hc.Failure(f"grilling: the registry of stage {stage} cannot be read (roles.json)")
    if not hubs:
        raise hc.UsageError(f"grilling: stage {stage} has no registered hub")
    if a.action == "status":
        m = grilling.active_stage(stage)
        print(f"grilling in progress in the hub of {stage} since {m['since']} ({m['source']})"
              + (f", topic: {m['topic']}" if m.get("topic") else "") + (f"; context ceiling reached {m['ceiling']}" if m.get("ceiling") else "")
              if m else f"no grilling in progress in the hub of {stage}")
        return 0
    if sid and sid not in hubs:
        raise hc.UsageError(f"grilling: session {sid[:8]} is not the hub of stage {stage} — only the registered hub's "
                            "grilling holds its handoff (the owner at a terminal: run it without a session)")
    at_terminal, sid = not sid, grilling.canonical(stage, sid or hubs[0])
    if a.action == "start":
        m = grilling.start(stage, sid, "hub grilling start", a.topic or "")
        print(f"grilling marked in progress in the hub of {stage} (session {sid[:8]}, since {m['since']}): automatic "
              f"handoffs wait for `hub grilling end --stage {stage}` (or {grilling.stale_seconds() // 60} min without "
              "an owner prompt)")
        return 0
    # the owner at a terminal ends the hub's mark under either of its ids
    gone = [m for m in (grilling.end(s, a.why or "") for s in (hubs if at_terminal else [sid])) if m]
    print(f"grilling ended in the hub of {stage}: automatic handoffs resume" if gone else
          f"no grilling was marked in the hub of {stage}: nothing to end")
    return 0


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- reviewer

def cmd_reviewer(a) -> int:
    helper_lines = hc.review_helper_lines()
    author = reviewers.parse_author(a.author, a.stage) if a.author else None
    host = engines.selected()
    if not author:  # never silent: the host's engine is a guess about who wrote the change
        hc.warn(f"author unknown: assuming the host engine ({host}) wrote the change; pass --author <role | engine[/model]> "
                "so the reviewer is chosen by who really wrote it")
    loaded = reviewers.load(author=author)
    for problem in loaded.problems:
        hc.warn(problem)
    verdicts, chosen = reviewers.walk(loaded, a.for_class, every=a.all, author=author)
    source = {"env": "the environment", "project": "the repository's .agent-hub/config.json",
              "home": "the hub home's config.json", "default": "the built-in default"}[loaded.origin]
    start = reviewers.start_line(chosen.entry, a.stage) if chosen else None
    if a.json:
        print(json.dumps({"class": a.for_class[:reviewers.SHOWN] if a.for_class else None, "source": loaded.origin,
                          "author": author.as_dict() if author else None, "assumed_author_engine": None if author else host,
                          "chosen": chosen.entry.name if chosen else None, "start": start, "helper_threshold": helper_lines,
                          "entries": [reviewers.entry_json(v) | ({"check_output": v.output} if a.all and v.output else {})
                                      for v in verdicts],
                          "invalid": loaded.problems}, ensure_ascii=False, indent=1))
        return 0 if chosen else 1
    print(f"author: {author} ({author.source})" if author else f"author: unknown, host engine {host} assumed")
    if a.all or not chosen:
        print(f"reviewers from {source}" + (f", change class {reviewers.show(a.for_class)}" if a.for_class else "") + ":")
        for v in verdicts:
            e = v.entry
            mark = "→" if chosen and v is chosen else " "
            print(f" {mark} {e.name} ({reviewers.describe(e)}): {'available' if v.available else 'not available'} — {v.why}")
            if a.all and v.output:
                print(f"     check output: {v.output}")
        if a.all:
            for problem in loaded.problems:
                print(f"   invalid: {problem}")
    if not chosen:
        print("no reviewer is available" + (f" for class {reviewers.show(a.for_class)}" if a.for_class else ""), file=sys.stderr)
        return 1
    e = chosen.entry
    print(f"reviewer: {e.name} ({reviewers.describe(e)})")
    print(f"review helpers: no judgement team below {helper_lines} changed lines. Fill this threshold in the brief")
    print(f"start: {start}")
    return 0


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- rename

def rename_strings(value, old: str, new: str, root: Path):
    """`value` (parsed JSON) with the stage's name replaced where it names the stage: a path under <hub home>/OLD, a
    title `Hub OLD #n…` or `… (OLD)`, a `stage` field. Other text is left as it is."""
    path_re = re.compile(re.escape(str(root / old)) + r"(?=/|$)")
    if isinstance(value, dict):
        return {k: (new if k == "stage" and v == old else rename_strings(v, old, new, root)) for k, v in value.items()}
    if isinstance(value, list):
        return [rename_strings(v, old, new, root) for v in value]
    if isinstance(value, str):
        text = path_re.sub(str(root / new), value).replace(f"Hub {old} #", f"Hub {new} #")
        return text[:-len(old) - 2] + f"({new})" if text.endswith(f"({old})") else text
    return value


def renamed_locks(locks: list, old: str, new: str, sessions: set) -> list:
    """[(index, new record)] of the board's locks whose notes name the stage: the holder is one of its sessions or the
    note carries `Hub OLD #` / starts `OLD:`; there the whole word OLD is replaced in owner_name, why and took_over_from
    (elsewhere only `Hub OLD #`: a lock of another stage that says it took over from this one)."""
    word = re.compile(rf"(?<![\w-]){re.escape(old)}(?![\w-])")
    out = []
    for i, lock in enumerate(locks):
        notes = {k: lock[k] for k in ("owner_name", "why", "took_over_from") if isinstance(lock.get(k), str)}
        own = lock.get("session_id") in sessions or any(
            f"Hub {old} #" in v or v.startswith(f"{old}:") for v in notes.values())
        changed = {k: (word.sub(new, v) if own else v.replace(f"Hub {old} #", f"Hub {new} #")) for k, v in notes.items()}
        if changed != notes:
            out.append((i, dict(lock, **changed)))
    return out


def cmd_rename(a) -> int:
    old = hc.check_stage(a.stage)
    if not a.to:
        raise hc.UsageError("rename: --to NEW is required")
    new = hc.check_stage(a.to)
    src, dst = hc.root() / old, hc.root() / new
    if old == new:
        raise hc.UsageError("rename: --to is the stage's own name")
    if not src.is_dir():
        raise hc.UsageError(f"no stage directory {src}")
    if dst.exists():
        raise hc.UsageError(f"stage {new} already exists ({dst})")
    if hc.naming_enforced() and (problem := hc.stage_name_problem(new)) is not None:
        raise hc.UsageError(problem)
    table = subagents.process_table()
    live = []
    for meta_path in sorted(src.glob("agents/*/meta.json")):
        try:
            meta = json.loads(meta_path.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            continue
        if isinstance(meta, dict) and subagents.is_alive(meta, table):
            live.append(f"{meta.get('role') or meta_path.parent.name} (pid {meta.get('pid')})")
    if live:
        raise hc.UsageError(f"stage {old} has live agents: {', '.join(live)} — stop them (`agent stop --stage {old} "
                            "<role>`) or wait until they finish, then rename")
    board = board_module()
    tag = "[plan] " if a.dry_run else ""
    undo = []  # what to put back, most recent first, when a step fails: the stage is then where and what it was
    # the roles lock is held from the first read to the end (and through a rollback): a `roles set` that lands in between
    # waits, instead of being overwritten by a snapshot taken before it
    with hc.roles_lock(old):
        files = [p for p in [*sorted(src.glob("*.json")), *sorted(src.glob("agents/*/meta.json"))] if p.is_file()]
        rewritten = {}  # relative path -> (text now, text after the rename): all read and checked before the first write
        for path in files:
            try:
                text = path.read_text(encoding="utf-8")
                data = json.loads(text)
            except (OSError, ValueError) as e:
                raise hc.Failure(f"{path} cannot be read as JSON ({e}); fix it by hand — nothing was renamed") from None
            rewritten[path.relative_to(src)] = (text, json.dumps(rename_strings(data, old, new, hc.root()),
                                                                  ensure_ascii=False, indent=1) + "\n")
        roles = hc.roles_load(old)["roles"]
        sessions = {v for r in roles.values() for v in (r.get("session"), r.get("cli_session_id")) if v}
        locks = board.load()
        lock_changes = renamed_locks(locks, old, new, sessions)
        register = src / "questions.md"
        register_text = register.read_text(encoding="utf-8") if register.is_file() else ""
        head, sep, rest = register_text.partition("\n")
        print(f"{tag}rename stage {old} → {new}: directory {src} → {dst}")
        print(f"{tag}rewrite names and paths in {len(files)} json file(s): " + ", ".join(str(p) for p in rewritten))
        for i, rec in lock_changes:
            print(f"{tag}board: {rec['kind']} ({rec.get('repo') or board.DEFAULT_REPO}): "
                  + "; ".join(f"{k} → {rec[k]!r}" for k in ("owner_name", "why", "took_over_from")
                              if rec.get(k) != locks[i].get(k)))
        if a.dry_run:
            return 0
        try:
            os.rename(src, dst)
            undo.append(lambda: os.rename(dst, src))
            for rel, (before, after) in rewritten.items():
                hc.atomic_write(dst / rel, after)
                undo.append(lambda rel=rel, before=before: hc.atomic_write(dst / rel, before))
            if head == f"# Owner questions — {old}":
                hc.atomic_write(dst / "questions.md", f"# Owner questions — {new}" + sep + rest)
                undo.append(lambda: hc.atomic_write(dst / "questions.md", register_text))
            if lock_changes:
                with board.Locked():
                    current = board.load()
                    for i, rec in renamed_locks(current, old, new, sessions):
                        current[i] = rec
                    board.write(current)
        except BaseException as e:  # also Ctrl-C and SIGTERM-as-exception: the stage must never stay half-renamed
            problems = []
            for step in reversed(undo):
                try:
                    step()
                except Exception as e2:  # keep undoing the rest
                    problems.append(str(e2))
            if not isinstance(e, Exception):
                print(f"rename {old} → {new} interrupted; " + ("rolled back" if not problems else
                      "ROLLBACK INCOMPLETE (" + "; ".join(problems) + ")"), file=sys.stderr)
                raise
            raise hc.Failure(f"rename {old} → {new} failed ({e}); " + ("rolled back" if not problems else
                             "ROLLBACK INCOMPLETE (" + "; ".join(problems) + ") — check " + f"{src} and {dst}")) from None
    print(f"renamed stage {old} → {new}. Sessions that still run under HUB_STAGE={old} (a hub, a shell) need the new name; "
          f"worktrees and branches named {old}-… are not renamed.")
    return 0


def cmd_effort(a) -> int:
    readings = session_effort.survey(resolve_self(a.session) if a.session else None)
    found = session_effort.best(readings)
    if a.json:
        print(json.dumps({"effort": found.effort if found else None, "source": found.source if found else None,
                          "readings": [r._asdict() for r in readings]}, ensure_ascii=False, indent=1))
    elif found:
        print(session_effort.describe(readings))
    if found is None:
        raise hc.Failure(session_effort.describe(readings))
    return 0


def cmd_home(a) -> int:
    if a.home_cmd == "migrate":
        return hubhome.migrate(a.src, a.dst, a.apply)
    return hubhome.show(a.cwd, a.json)


# ---------------------------------------------------------------- close

def live_agents(stage: str, table) -> list:
    """[(role, meta)] of the stage's `agent spawn` agents whose process runs."""
    out = []
    for meta_path in sorted((hc.root() / stage).glob("agents/*/meta.json")):
        try:
            meta = json.loads(meta_path.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            continue
        if isinstance(meta, dict) and subagents.is_alive(meta, table):
            out.append((meta.get("role") or meta_path.parent.name, meta))
    return out


def waiting_questions(stage: str) -> list:
    """The stage's owner questions that still wait for the owner (open, or default taken), as "id title" strings."""
    try:
        _, entries = ask_module().load(stage)
    except BaseException as e:  # noqa: BLE001 — `ask` exits on a broken register: a close must not pass it unread
        raise hc.Failure(f"the question register of {stage} is unreadable ({e}); fix it (`ask list --stage {stage}`)") from None
    return [f"{e.id} {e.title}" for e in entries if e.kind_letter == "Q" and e.state in ("open", "default-taken")]


def stage_lock_sessions(data: dict) -> dict:
    """{session id: role} of every role of the stage, live and retired — the sessions whose locks the stage holds. A
    retired one counts: an agent `agent stop` retired (also by a close that died before its locks were released), an
    earlier hub whose lock nobody took over."""
    out = {}
    recs = [(rec.get("role"), rec) for rec in data.get("retired", [])] + list(data.get("roles", {}).items())
    for role, rec in recs:   # live roles last: their names win
        for sid in (rec.get("session"), rec.get("cli_session_id")):
            if isinstance(sid, str) and sid:
                out[sid] = role or "?"
    return out


def held_elsewhere(sid: str, stage: str) -> str:
    """Why the session `sid` must be left alone ("" when nothing holds it): it still plays a live role in another open
    stage (its locks and its process are that stage's too), or the other stages' registries could not all be read."""
    hits, complete = registry_of(sid)
    other = next((h[0] for h in hits if h[3] and h[0] != stage and not hc.stage_closed(h[0])), "")
    if other:
        return f"it is live in stage {other}"
    return "" if complete else "a registry of another stage could not be read"


def closed_hub_tag(stage: str, rec: dict) -> str:
    """The tag of the hub being closed: the registered one, else (a re-run after the roles were retired) the latest
    retired `hub` record's — so the hub that reopens the stage continues the numbering."""
    if rec.get("tag"):
        return rec["tag"]
    retired = [r for r in hc.roles_load(stage)["retired"] if r.get("role") == "hub" and r.get("tag")]
    return retired[-1]["tag"] if retired else ""


def cmd_close(a) -> int:
    """`hub close`: the stage's work is over — its hub is no longer needed (see the help). The summary line comes first
    (agent-top shows the first line; it carries the ATTENTION when the hub session still runs), the steps after it; a
    failed step prints the steps done before the error."""
    lines: list = []
    try:
        summary = close_stage(a, lines.append)
    except BaseException:
        if lines:
            print("\n".join(lines))
        raise
    print("\n".join([summary, *lines]))
    return 0


def close_stage(a, say) -> str:
    stage = hc.check_stage(a.stage)
    if not (hc.root() / stage).is_dir():
        raise hc.UsageError(f"no stage {stage} in {hc.root()}")
    closed = hc.stage_closed(stage)
    if closed:
        return (f"stage {stage} is already closed ({closed.get('at')}: {closed.get('why')}); "
                f"`hub takeover --stage {stage} --session …` reopens it")
    why = hc.one_line(a.why or "") or "no longer needed"
    me = hc.session_id()
    live = [(role, meta) for role, meta in live_agents(stage, subagents.process_table())
            if not me or me != meta.get("session_id")]  # a headless hub closing its own stage does not stop itself
    questions = waiting_questions(stage)
    blockers = []
    if live and not a.force:
        blockers.append("live agents: " + ", ".join(f"{r} (pid {m.get('pid')})" for r, m in live)
                        + f" — stop them (`agent stop --stage {stage} <role>`) or wait until they finish")
    if questions and not a.force:
        blockers.append(f"owner questions still waiting: {'; '.join(questions)} — record the answer (`ask close`) or "
                        "withdraw them (`ask withdraw <id> --reason …`)")
    if blockers:
        raise hc.UsageError(f"stage {stage} is not closed — " + "; ".join(blockers)
                            + ". --force stops the agents and leaves the questions in the register")
    plan = "[plan] " if a.dry_run else ""
    notes, attention = [], []
    # what the stage is now, read before anything stops: `agent stop` retires its agent's role, and the locks of that
    # agent's session are the stage's all the same
    data = hc.roles_load(stage)
    hub_rec = data["roles"].get("hub") or {}
    sessions = stage_lock_sessions(data)
    sessions.update({m["session_id"]: r for r, m in live if isinstance(m.get("session_id"), str) and m["session_id"]})

    # 1. live agents (only with --force): stopped through `agent stop`, which also retires their roles
    for role, meta in live:
        if a.dry_run:
            say(f"[plan] stop agent {role} (pid {meta.get('pid')}): agent stop --stage {stage} {role}")
            continue
        try:
            res = subprocess.run([str(hc.BIN / "agent"), "stop", "--stage", stage, role], capture_output=True,
                                 text=True, timeout=60, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL)
        except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError) as e:
            raise hc.Failure(f"stopping agent {role} failed ({e}); the stage is not closed — re-run when it is stopped") from None
        if res.returncode != 0:
            raise hc.Failure(f"`agent stop --stage {stage} {role}` exited {res.returncode}: "
                             f"{(res.stderr or res.stdout).strip()[:300]}; the stage is not closed")
        say(f"stopped agent {role}")
    if live:
        notes.append(f"{'would stop' if a.dry_run else 'stopped'} agents {', '.join(r for r, _ in live)}")
    if questions:
        notes.append(f"{len(questions)} owner question(s) left waiting in the register")
        say(f"ATTENTION: {len(questions)} owner question(s) stay in the register, hidden from the summaries while "
            f"the stage is closed: {'; '.join(questions)}")
    jtag = hc.caller_tag(stage) or "owner"  # a terminal or the agent-top pane: the owner closes it

    # 2. the hub's session: a background one that is idle is stopped, any other is named with how to end it; one that
    # still plays a live role in another open stage (or may: a registry unread) is that stage's and is left alone
    hub_ids = [x for x in (hub_rec.get("session"), hub_rec.get("cli_session_id")) if isinstance(x, str) and x]
    busy_elsewhere = next((w for w in map(lambda x: held_elsewhere(x, stage), hub_ids) if w), "")
    if busy_elsewhere:
        say(f"left the hub session {hub_ids[0]} running: {busy_elsewhere}")
        notes.append(f"hub session left running ({busy_elsewhere})")
    else:
        stopped, running = replaced_hub(hub_rec, "", "", stage, a.dry_run, label="the stage's hub")
        if stopped:
            say(stopped)
            notes.append(stopped.removeprefix("[plan] "))
        if running:
            say(f"ATTENTION: {running}")
            attention.append(running)
            notes.append(running)

    # 3. locks held by the stage's sessions, except a session another open stage still holds (see held_elsewhere)
    board = board_module()
    released, kept = [], []
    with board.Locked():
        locks = board.load()
        drop = []
        for rec in locks:
            sid = rec.get("session_id")
            if sid not in sessions:
                continue
            name = f"{rec['kind']} ({rec.get('repo') or board.DEFAULT_REPO})"
            reason = held_elsewhere(sid, stage)
            if reason:
                kept.append(f"{name}: its holder {sessions[sid]} — {reason}")
            else:
                drop.append(rec)
                released.append(name)
        if drop and not a.dry_run:
            board.write([r for r in locks if not any(r is d for d in drop)])
    for name in released:
        say(f"{plan}released lock {name}")
    for k in kept:
        say(f"kept lock {k}")

    # 4.–5. under the stage's roles lock, from the check to the mark: every role retired, the journal line, the mark. A
    # takeover that registered a new hub meanwhile wins (nothing retired, exit 1); one that comes after waits for the
    # lock, then finds the stage closed and reopens it. The mark is last: a re-run after a failure finds the stage open.
    retired = sorted(data["roles"])
    text = ""
    with (contextlib.nullcontext() if a.dry_run else hc.roles_lock(stage)):
        cur = hc.roles_load(stage)
        now_hub = cur["roles"].get("hub") or {}
        # a hub that is gone is the one stopped above (`agent stop hub` retires it); only another one is a takeover
        if not a.dry_run and now_hub and now_hub.get("session") != hub_rec.get("session"):
            raise hc.Failure(f"stage {stage} got a new hub while it was being closed ({now_hub.get('title') or now_hub.get('session')}); "
                             f"its roles are kept and the stage stays open — locks released: {', '.join(released) or 'none'}")
        hub_tag = closed_hub_tag(stage, hub_rec)
        if not a.dry_run:
            at = hc.now().isoformat(timespec="seconds")
            retired = sorted(cur["roles"])
            for role, rec in sorted(cur["roles"].items()):
                cur["retired"].append(dict(rec, role=role, retired_at=at, retired_why=f"stage closed: {why}"))
            if retired:
                cur["roles"] = {}
                hc.roles_save(stage, cur)
        if retired:
            say(f"{plan}retired roles: {', '.join(retired)}")
        text = (f"close: stage {stage} closed — {why}; locks released: {', '.join(released) or 'none'}"
                + (f"; locks kept: {', '.join(kept)}" if kept else "")
                + f"; roles retired: {', '.join(retired) or 'none'}" + ("; " + "; ".join(notes) if notes else ""))
        if not a.dry_run:
            hc.journal_append(stage, jtag, text)
            hc.record_stage_closed(stage, {"at": hc.now().isoformat(timespec="seconds"), "why": why, "by": me or "owner",
                                           "hub": hub_tag})
    if a.dry_run:
        say(f"[plan] journal [{jtag}] {text}")
        say(f"[plan] mark the stage closed in {hc.root() / stage / hc.STAGE_FILE}")
        return f"[plan] close stage {stage}: {why} (dry run: nothing was written)" + "".join(f" ATTENTION: {w}" for w in attention)
    return (f"closed stage {stage}: {why}." + "".join(f" ATTENTION: {w}" for w in attention)
            + f" Hidden from agent-top (--all shows it), the watchdog and the summaries; "
            f"`hub takeover --stage {stage} --session …` reopens it.")


def main(argv: list) -> int:
    p = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="hub", description=__doc__, formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter)
    sub = p.add_subparsers(dest="cmd", required=True)
    stage_opt = argparse.ArgumentParser(add_help=False)  # every subcommand takes it: one habit, no "unrecognized arguments"
    stage_opt.add_argument("--stage", help="the stage (default: $HUB_STAGE)")
    st = sub.add_parser("start", parents=[stage_opt], help="register the first hub of a new stage")
    st.add_argument("--session", required=True, help="your full session id (local_… or a CLI uuid)")
    st.add_argument("--n", type=int, help=argparse.SUPPRESS)
    st.add_argument("--goal", help="one line: what the stage delivers, in the owner's words (required for a new stage; "
                                   "kept in the stage directory, shown in the hub's title, the digest and agent-top)")
    st.add_argument("--name", help="title (default: \"Hub <stage> #1 — <goal>\")")
    st.add_argument("--main-merge-until", default="+30d", help="main-merge expiry with --take-main-merge")
    st.add_argument("--take-main-merge", action="store_true", help="also take main-merge of this repository")
    st.add_argument("--skip-lock", action="append", metavar="RESOURCE", help="leave this lock where it is (repeatable)")
    st.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true")
    st.add_argument("--repo", metavar="PATH", help="the project's repository (any path inside it) when the working "
                                                   "directory is not in one; default: the stage's recorded project")
    st.add_argument("--no-project", action="store_true", help="the stage has no repository: start in place")
    t = sub.add_parser("takeover", parents=[stage_opt], help="take over the hub role")
    t.add_argument("--n", type=int, help="number of the new hub (default: derived from roles.json / the handoff)")
    t.add_argument("--session", required=True, help="full session id of the new hub (local_… or a CLI uuid; `self` = "
                                                     "$CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID)")
    t.add_argument("--handoff", help="handoff file (default: the latest HANDOFF-hub-*.md)")
    t.add_argument("--goal", help="set or replace the stage's goal line (default: the one kept by `hub start`)")
    t.add_argument("--name", help="title (default: \"Hub <stage> #<n> — <goal>\")")
    t.add_argument("--skip-lock", action="append", metavar="RESOURCE",
                   help="leave this lock with the previous hub (repeatable)")
    t.add_argument("--main-merge-until", default="+30d", help="main-merge expiry when taken from nobody")
    t.add_argument("--take-main-merge", action="store_true",
                   help="also take main-merge when it is free or held by a third party")
    t.add_argument("--auto-handoff", action="store_true",
                   help="this is the successor `hub succeed` started (its prompt gives the command): keeps the chain of "
                        "automatic handoffs, which any other takeover resets")
    t.add_argument("--desktop-request", help="reservation token in the desktop successor brief")
    t.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true")
    t.add_argument("--repo", metavar="PATH", help="the project's repository (any path inside it) when the working "
                                                  "directory is not in one; default: the stage's recorded project")
    t.add_argument("--no-project", action="store_true", help="the stage has no repository: take over in place")
    h = sub.add_parser("handoff", parents=[stage_opt], help="write a handoff draft")
    h.add_argument("--n", type=int, help="number of the outgoing hub (default: the registered hub's)")
    h.add_argument("--out")
    h.add_argument("--session", help="the hub's session whose sub-agents are checked (default: the registered hub's)")
    h.add_argument("--allow-live-subagents", action="store_true",
                   help="write the draft although sub-agents of the hub still run; the list goes into its TODO")
    h.add_argument("--finish", action="store_true",
                   help="do not write a draft: check the filled one (--handoff, else the latest) and refuse while § 0–2 hold TODO")
    h.add_argument("--handoff", help="with --finish: the handoff to check (default: the latest HANDOFF-hub-*.md)")
    h.add_argument("--allow-todo", action="store_true", help="with --finish: accept a handoff with TODO left in § 0–2")
    h.add_argument("--owner-asked", action="store_true",
                   help="the owner asked for this handoff: write it although a grilling is in progress (it carries the grilling)")
    sc = sub.add_parser("succeed", parents=[stage_opt], help="start the successor of an automatic handoff (autopilot)")
    sc.add_argument("--handoff", help="the filled handoff draft")
    sc.add_argument("--allow-todo", action="store_true", help="start the successor although § 0–2 of the handoff still hold TODO")
    sc.add_argument("--model", help="the successor's model (default: AGENT_HUB_SUCCESSOR_MODEL, else the hub's own)")
    sc.add_argument("--effort", choices=tuple(dict.fromkeys(hc.EFFORTS + engines.CODEX_EFFORTS)),
                    help="the successor's effort (default: AGENT_HUB_SUCCESSOR_EFFORT, else this hub's own effort, read "
                         "from its session — see `hub effort`; refused when that cannot be read)")
    sc.add_argument("--permission-mode", help="the successor's mode (default: AGENT_HUB_SUCCESSOR_PERMISSION_MODE, "
                                              "else default)")
    sc.add_argument("--cwd", help="the successor's working directory (default: here)")
    sc.add_argument("--engine", choices=engines.ENGINES, help="successor engine (default: current host)")
    sc.add_argument("--surface", choices=("auto", "desktop", "cli"), default="auto",
                    help="Codex launch surface: app -> native request; app CLI requires home owner opt-in; console/worker -> CLI")
    sc.add_argument("--desktop-worktree", action="store_true", help="native worktree only when explicitly requested by the owner")
    sc.add_argument("--branch", help="desktop worktree starting branch, only when explicitly requested and existing")
    sc.add_argument("--headless", action="store_true", help="start a headless hub (agent spawn); from Codex Desktop requires home owner opt-in")
    sc.add_argument("--fallback", action="store_true", help="the background successor did not take over: stop it "
                                                            "and start a headless one")
    sc.add_argument("--why", help="with --fallback: the reason for the journal")
    sc.add_argument("--again", action="store_true", help="the recorded successor did not take over and is not running: "
                                                         "drop its record and start a new one")
    sc.add_argument("--replace", action="store_true",
                    help="replace the successor that already took over (or runs): stop it (`claude stop`; not while it is "
                         "busy, unless --force) and start a new one from the same handoff with the same number and chain "
                         "position. For the hub that handed over, or the owner at a terminal")
    sc.add_argument("--force", action="store_true", help="run although AGENT_HUB_AUTO_HANDOFF is off (the owner, by hand); "
                                                          "with --replace: also stop a successor that is busy")
    sc.add_argument("--owner-asked", action="store_true",
                    help="the owner asked for this handoff: start the successor although a grilling is in progress")
    sc.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true")
    gp = sub.add_parser("grilling", parents=[stage_opt], help="mark that the hub is grilling the owner: no automatic "
                                                              "handoff until it ends")
    gp.add_argument("action", choices=("start", "end", "status"))
    gp.add_argument("--session", help="the hub's session (default: this one; at a terminal: the registered hub's)")
    gp.add_argument("--topic", help="with start: the topic, for the journal and the handoff")
    gp.add_argument("--why", help="with end: why it ended (frontier empty, the owner stopped it), for the journal")
    dr = sub.add_parser("desktop-request", help="reserve native dispatch and print create_thread args for a saved project")
    db = sub.add_parser("desktop-bind", help="confirm native client/actual identity without claiming takeover")
    df = sub.add_parser("desktop-fail", help="record native failure without an invisible CLI fallback")
    ds = sub.add_parser("desktop-status", help="show requested/observed identity and verified takeover")
    dc = sub.add_parser("desktop-recover", help="repair proven same-shift native identity from the current app hub")
    ds.add_argument("--verified", action="store_true", help="exit 1 until the actual takeover verifies")
    for dp in (dr, db, df, ds, dc):
        dp.add_argument("--stage", required=True)
        dp.add_argument("--request", required=True)
    dr.add_argument("--project-id", required=True)
    dr.add_argument("--project-path", required=True)
    db.add_argument("--project-id")
    db.add_argument("--thread-id")
    db.add_argument("--client-thread-id")
    df.add_argument("--why", required=True)
    df.add_argument("--no-thread-created", action="store_true", help="confirmed failure before any thread creation")
    rn = sub.add_parser("rename", parents=[stage_opt], help="rename a stage that has no live agent")
    rn.add_argument("--to", metavar="NEW", help="the new stage name (it must name the work, like `hub start`'s)")
    rn.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true")
    cl = sub.add_parser("close", parents=[stage_opt], help="close a stage whose hub is no longer needed")
    cl.add_argument("--why", help="one line for the journal and stage.json (default: no longer needed)")
    cl.add_argument("--force", action="store_true",
                    help="close with live agents (they are stopped) or owner questions still waiting (they stay)")
    cl.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true")
    ef = sub.add_parser("effort", parents=[stage_opt], help="the effort a session runs at now, and where it was read")
    ef.add_argument("--session", help="a CLI session uuid or a Desktop local_… id (default: this session)")
    ef.add_argument("--json", action="store_true", help="every source's reading as JSON")
    r = sub.add_parser("reviewer", parents=[stage_opt], help="choose the reviewer for a change and print how to start it "
                       "(with a stage, the `agent spawn` line carries --stage)")
    r.add_argument("--for", dest="for_class", metavar="CLASS", help="the change's class (docs, code, risky, …)")
    r.add_argument("--author", metavar="ROLE|ENGINE[/MODEL]",
                   help="who wrote the change: a role of the stage (its engine and model are read from the agent's "
                        "meta.json) or claude|codex[/model]; the reviewer is chosen by it, not by the host's engine. "
                        "Checks see AGENT_HUB_REVIEW_AUTHOR_ENGINE / _MODEL")
    r.add_argument("--all", action="store_true", help="judge and list every entry, not only up to the first available")
    r.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    ho = sub.add_parser("home", parents=[stage_opt], help="where the hub keeps its files; `home migrate` moves them "
                        "(--stage is accepted, the hub home does not depend on it)")
    ho.add_argument("--cwd", help="resolve for this directory (default: here)")
    ho.add_argument("--json", action="store_true")
    hos = ho.add_subparsers(dest="home_cmd")
    hm = hos.add_parser("migrate", parents=[stage_opt], help="move the hub home (default: the legacy ~/.claude/agent-hub to the resolved one)")
    hm.add_argument("--from", dest="src", metavar="DIR", help="default: ~/.claude/agent-hub")
    hm.add_argument("--to", dest="dst", metavar="DIR", help="default: the resolved hub home (~/agent-hub when that is "
                                                            "the source)")
    hm.add_argument("--apply", action="store_true", help="do it (default: a dry run)")
    grill_session.add_parser(sub, stage_opt)
    a = p.parse_args(argv)
    a.argv = list(argv)  # a MOVE message repeats the command line
    explicit, a.stage = a.stage, a.stage or os.environ.get("HUB_STAGE") or None
    needs_stage = a.cmd in ("start", "takeover", "handoff", "succeed", "rename", "close", "grill")
    if needs_stage and not a.stage:
        p.error(f"{a.cmd}: --stage is required (or set HUB_STAGE)")
    if a.stage and not hc.STAGE_RE.fullmatch(a.stage):  # check_stage does the rest for the commands that use the stage
        if explicit or needs_stage:
            p.error(f"bad stage name {a.stage!r} (lowercase letters, digits, '-' and '_')")
        a.stage = None  # a stray HUB_STAGE does not break `reviewer` and `home`, which never needed it
    return {"start": cmd_start, "takeover": cmd_takeover, "handoff": cmd_handoff, "succeed": cmd_succeed,
            "reviewer": cmd_reviewer, "home": cmd_home, "effort": cmd_effort, "rename": cmd_rename,
            "close": cmd_close, "grill": grill_session.main, "grilling": cmd_grilling,
            "desktop-recover": lambda a: autopilot.desktop_recover(hc.check_stage(a.stage), a.request),
            "desktop-status": lambda a: autopilot.desktop_status(hc.check_stage(a.stage), a.request, a.verified),
            "desktop-request": lambda a: autopilot.desktop_request(hc.check_stage(a.stage), a.request, a.project_id, a.project_path),
            "desktop-bind": lambda a: autopilot.desktop_bind(hc.check_stage(a.stage), a.request, a.thread_id, a.client_thread_id, a.project_id),
            "desktop-fail": lambda a: autopilot.desktop_fail(hc.check_stage(a.stage), a.request, a.why, a.no_thread_created)}[a.cmd](a)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    raise SystemExit(hc.run_main(main, sys.argv[1:]))
